<$transclude $variable="table" $mode="block"/>

</$let>

''Holders'' (2026-11-18, by the division of #/rulings): every rank above names its holder where a backlog holds it; rank 16's flat-store o-takiage parks in backlog-alpha #/next. Held by neither backlog yet, each waiting for the controller's fold: rank 2's bytes-at-rest slice, rank 2a's `bin/sync` comparison, rank 4d (a) and (c), rank 4k's T4-1, T4-3, T4-4 and T4-8, `C1`'s adapter (rank 6), and the WAVE TWO and AFTER ranks from 7 onward that name no holder.

''Deferred deeply'' (operator, 2026-11-18: //"2 minor things we need to deeply defer: installing on Freyja's PC, and 'release'"//; #/rulings). DEFERRED: Freyja's install and its first live walk; the walk (lar:///ha.ka.ba/wsl2/new-hearth) stays in canon and keeps truing as rulings land, no lane schedules the install, and the house preflight and the hard-coded paths in backlog-alpha #/next stand on their own merit, never as its gate; rank 4h's flip reads the operator's own house alone. DEFERRED: the first release from `main` (naming, cadence, what a release carries, the image and genesis bake per release of rank 3, the queue's pull request from `develop` to `main`); its draft rests for the day it wakes and no lane schedules it. Neither moves a rank: each wakes on the operator's word.

''The evergreen keep'' (operator, 2026-11-16: //"approve the defaults, keep flowing; true up the roadmap memes."//; design lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/evergreen-keep): two layers stand, the ''keep'' (plaintext, content-addressed, point-in-time, one document's record set per unit under a house manifest, surviving every re-founding) and the ''replica'' (a per-document CRDT peer on a fleet device, for availability alone, riding `C7` and `C2`), with no change log between them. `K1`, `K2` and `K11` land before the merge (rank 2a); `K3` and `K5` land in WAVE TWO ahead of `L35` (rank 16); `K4`, `K6` to `K10` land where ranks 13b, 13d, 15a and 29a seat them. Four forks stand on their rulings: F1 cleartext wherever the operator's own hands hold the copy, sealed past them; F2 no cross-revision bridge (restore at the cut's revision, walk forward by kūkulu); F3 a second operator-held remote when the operator names one, no code owed; F4 keys return through `vault backup` and `vault restore`, past `M8`.

''Wave two beside the dogfooding.'' Wave two holds ten items, with `K3`, `K4`, `K5` and `K6` (ranks 13b to 13d) beside them, with `C15` beside `C2`, the first three things (`L40` to `L42`, ranks 9a to 9c) and the clock loop (rank 9d) beside them, and `L49` (rank 13a) after the tiddler door's relay; a letter rank seats an item between two integers so the ranks other carriers cite stay put. `C1`'s second cut, `C2`, `C9` and `C10` run as four builders (the host shim's own wiring in `C10` stays the controller's hand, and spirits never touch the shim); `L17-2a` and `L17-2b` take the next two slots, `L17-2c` follows `2b`, and `L17-2d` rides the controller's own hand on this carrier. Until `C1`'s second cut lands, a dogfood day that lights several faces shows them together to a peer that reads the wire; until `C9` lands, the browser leg rests on an honest page.

''Merged'', each into the item named: the browser reset item of the rite's ledger into `C4`; the shared Kahu-cabal workbench item and Leap 2b into `P21`; `L16` into `C3`; Leaps 2a and 3's device-A share meeting a device-B mount into `C7`; the integer `boundEpoch` leap, `L32` and Leap 0's tail into one epoch burn (rank 18); `K22`'s review into `C6`; `T37`'s keyslot zeroing into `C9`; the browser surface's passphrase-leak item into `C9`; the after-founding comms into rank 31; after-the-seat's declared-tier share gate bullet into `P27`; Leap 6 into ranks 3 and 4, the carry rite walking the proof on the operator's own house; the AI's memory frame and the kahua two-tier lift into `L35`.

''Items this survey could not judge'', each ranked as its item reads until a lane re-measures it: `L4f` (whether a joined own-hearth page mounts the daemon document; the fourth rehearsal's page write as face 1 reached no hearth file in eight seconds, which `C15` carries); `T23` (the leaf fleet's reload-clean seat, `3fcdfd85e`, may cure it, and no red re-ran); the veil and leaf tails' "persona roots key by PersonaGroup" (`db71539d6` files a browser root under its face's own tree, while the node's `listPersonaRoots` and face ordinals stay unread); the record batches' owed lists of #/rulings, most older than `clock-sweep`, `b5b` and the lifts (`STORE_DOOR_PHASES` still decides a refusal by wall clock in `store-door.ts`; the rest stand unread); `M2`'s "slices 6 and 7", which no item names an owner for; whether the shared-holder mode, and with it the holder-protocol restart, outlived the browser vessel lift; many floors beyond the vessel floor lane's own statement.

''Beside the ranks'': GROUND's items, HARBOR's tail on the operator's hands, and DreamDOM's train D on its own files (its `D18` keeps each surface's twin of `C4`, its `D19` rides rank 15).

