<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-leaps`>>

!! The leaps ~ the walk to the dogfood stand, in flowstate (operator, 2026-11-11)

Each leap lands a whole model under the gate of #/rulings (2026-11-11, the leaps run in flowstate); its law lives in the carrier it names, and this section keeps the order and the items still owed. Landed work reads in git and its commit trailers (`node tools/changelog-render.mjs <from>..<to>`); the lanes in flight and their heads read in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff#/state`>>; #/the-order ranks every leap still owed.

!!! Landed, one line each
* ''Leap 0, the clockless sweep'' (`e2fc2158c`, its bake `6d2f476f3`): no version literal, a KEL ordered by hash-chain descent with `seq` as a cross-check, a floor announcement linked by `prior`, the IndexedDB version a pinned platform constant.
* ''Leap 1, the vessel floor and its accept'' (`63bc695d9`, with its bake): <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane#/the-vessel-pin`>>; its owed items rest in that carrier's #/owed.
* ''Leaps 2a and 3, the private workbench and the workspaces'' (`952f50dec`): <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/the-workbench`>>.
* ''Leap 4, the offering door'' (`312c2f2a0`, with its bake): <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/offering`>>.
* ''Leap 5, the canon true-up'' (`3156b4e94`), and the pre-walk lane (`07d53bdc4`, its bake `5a8b5e603`) with the test-typecheck ratchet (`8843a8eff`).
* ''The veil floor and the leaf fleet'' (merged `4c38d53d5` and `cef201dac`, their bake `cd4a04f46`): <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/the-veil-ladder#/the-base-model`>>, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/device-capabilities-2026#/device-seats`>>.
* ''The contract build'' (`490d2b040`, `105773654`, `13fa40151`, its bake `ce48376c1`): one workbench for a wiki on a vessel, one folder for a workbench, and every carry act following the document: <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/the-workbench`>>.
* ''The veil's first cut'' (`110804ead..7ba75df75`): a store id for each worn face, a peer id for each composition, an offer keyed at its Nexus, a salted recovery commitment (`C1`).
* ''The carry residue'' (`c28a77478..7bc2e42fb`): a kahua act rides its own face's wear (`kahua-face-unworn`), the daemon island mounts the pinned floor, a share landing counts what moved, every carry act names its waits and accounts for every record, and the runbook's release and carry blocks read as a walked hearth answered them (`C8`; its open item rides `C15`).
* ''The browser's confirm gate'' (`ca1a989b6..f7ff6827c`): the reset proves the holder's passphrase at rest before anything burns (`C4`).
* ''The TiddlyWiki caps, phase 1'' (`6ef0e3d61..567b3d518`, `b3b9a7654..1c64c2781`): one family law with the orphan folder and its flag, and the tiddler door on the anchor with its delete's two modes, joined to the family law (`9228064ba`, `96b6e59a3`; `L17`).
* ''The mirror, whole'': the glass theme (`00c7af858`), the floor's replay into every island and the pane as viewport (`18c05e779`, `a8f6058d0`), the whole handoff and the doors (`231e0c6a4`, `2eeef99fe`), and the module holds CI asked for (`7ebcb57d7`, `c09ebfdce`): <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/d3-glass-lane#/the-handoff`>>.

!!! The leaps of 2026-11-12 still owed
# ''The integer `boundEpoch` retires'' (#/rulings, 2026-11-12, lean 2): every edge, its readers and its census name the PersonaGroup lineage head digest; supersession by acts; a hard break forks. It merges with `L32`'s last slice and Leap 0's tail into one epoch burn (#/the-order, rank 18).
# ''A hearth founds as an existing face'' (#/rulings, 2026-11-12, lean 3): the node's `found` path with no face 0, its veil floor, the carriage join to F, the seed charter sealed as F, and the node's seat verbs (`lares fleet seat request|grant|land`). The first fleet offer founding the face and a second face founded later in one browser ride it (#/the-order, rank 20).
# ''Many floors in one recipe'' (#/rulings, 2026-11-12, many floors): the recipe stacks a vessel's floor pins innermost-first, one per Nexus; today the pool mounts a sole pin and two pins disagreeing mount genesis (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane#/many-floors`>>; #/the-order, rank 26).
Leap 6, the proof: the cold rehearsals on scratch roots walked the live rite, the operator's own walk with its browser leg re-founded the dogfood hearth, and the carry rite walks the proof again at PR #218's merge (#/the-order, ranks 3 and 4). Leap 2b, the cross-operator workbench, rides `P21` (#/after-the-seat).

!!! The leaps of 2026-11-14 ~ residency follows the contract, the TiddlyWiki caps as phases, the memory stage primary
The talk-story of 2026-11-14 settled the residency model (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/residency-follows-the-contract`>>), the wiki-surface scout's lean stands approved (operator, 2026-11-14: //"Pono!!! I approve all!"//; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-surface-scout#/phases`>>), and the rehearsals and the contract build handed back their residue. Each item names what it proves, its reds where its source names them, and what it waits on; #/the-order ranks it. Train letter ''C'' names the contract leaps.
* `C1` ''The veil at the wire, the second cut'' (operator-approved, 2026-11-14; wave two; the first cut as it stands, the three switches and every seam that still shows faces together rest in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/residency-follows-the-contract#/faces-sit-flat`>>). STANDS on each vessel's legs: each seated leg presents the alias of its (face, Nexus) and rests an inbound store id under that pair's scope, keeping resumption (`WireIdentity.leg`, `wire-legs.ts`); the node's client dial and the browser's relay seat through one door (`seatDialLeg`); the sibling channel's peer id takes the face (`siblingPeerIdOf`) and its metadata seats as the leg of its (face, Nexus) (`seatSiblingLeg`). Owed: a gate for each (face, Nexus), since one gate for each Nexus answers a contracted peer as one hearth for every face there; a walked test where a session switches onto a lit face and one where `vault unlock --all` lights three; the browser's presence broadcast of one vessel key under every face (`open-browser-vessel.ts`, `afterLive`) leaves, or goes per face; the Keyhive contact-card exchange at a sibling's light (`operator-daemon-behavior.ts`) runs only where a share entry names the pair; a rotation that reveals the contacts' keys; the genesis recovery commitment, unsalted while `provisionThresholdRecoveryAtFounding` holds no caller. Reds: a peer seated under face 0 reads a lit face 1's ids as unrelated to face 0's; a session switch onto a lit face presents that face's ids; one face shows two store ids at two Nexuses. Controls: one face's two connections at one Nexus read one id, and resumption across a restart holds. The acceptance tests W1 to W4 cover neither a lit sibling nor a session switch. Unwalked yet: the three switches (read, never walked), an offer on a hearth under the keyed offer body, a recovery, a browser hearth. The adapter opens the ONE FACE band (#/the-order, rank 34).
* `C2` ''The realm's key: the rest gate'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/the-workbench`>>). A vessel seals the working document of the wiki it mounts under the worn face's own content key, so a face seated in ANOTHER face's realm on the same vessel cannot open that rest; it mounts no workbench there and writes its own `personal` layer (`workbench-seat` answers `restsUnderOwner`). A wiki the vessel does not mount rests its workbench outside any face's seal. ''The house's decision'' (2026-11-14, overrulable, its reason recorded): of the three roads the contract build named, the workbench bag's content key wraps for its realm's roster, through the lockbox the content-key seat already runs (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/the-store`>>). The operator ruled //"Other wikis should get shared/contracted crdt doc caps"//, and only the roster's wrap carries to a second vessel and a second operator: a rest sealed under its owner's key opens only while that owner stands lit on the one vessel that holds the key, and dies with the owner's departure; a rest sealed under the vessel's key opens for no seat on any other vessel and for every face of this one, seated or not. The same wrap seals the unmounted wiki's workbench for its roster. Reds: a face seated `write` in another face's realm on one vessel mounts that wiki's workbench, its put answers `"layer":"working"`, and the owner reads the page after a restart; the rest of an unmounted wiki's workbench opens for no face its roster leaves out. Controls: an unseated face still writes `personal`; a face the share stops naming loses its seat by the convergent revoke, and its next save refuses `workbench-not-a-member`. Wave two.
* `P21` widened, the Kahu realm's workbench: the item in #/after-the-seat.
* `C3` ''The seed source slot'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/residency-follows-the-contract#/two-workspaces`>>; operator, 2026-11-14: //"Git serves only Amorphous Dreams Cabal Kahu, other local nexus operators with their own private/public/contracted realms will probably seed from npms or other stores or even from the DreamNet itself."//). One slot names canon's seed source, with four fillers: the checkout's `bags/`, a package's baked genesis floor, another store, and the DreamNet's release board, so a hearth with no checkout founds by the same road. It carries `L16`, the non-dev install (`LARES_WORKSPACE` naming a corpus directory with no repository, seeded from the image's genesis and release bags). Reds: a scratch corpus with no `.git` founds, stands and projects with its slot naming the package floor, and reads house canon by CID; control: the checkout filler writes back into the tracked `bags/` as today. Waits on nothing.
* `C4` ''The critical-procedure confirm gate'' (#/rulings, 2026-11-13; the browser's gate as it stands: <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/browser-vessel-lift#/the-confirm-gate`>>). Owed: the host reset gate (`C10`); the passkey and paper routes at the gate; the face and place clears that spend no gate pass (`clearFaceCustody`, `clearBrowserCustody`, `browserFleetJoinAbandon`); whether any-tree-opens narrows to the place tree; the gate on the other vessels' doors that destroy a place or a face; the ceremony-entry witness's header line about the worker; an error line at the browser reset for a wrong passphrase, which refuses `no-slot-opens` and showed the holder nothing in the fifth rehearsal. DreamDOM's `D18` keeps each surface's twin.
* `C5` ''The Handle that keeps the veil'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/residency-follows-the-contract#/a-cabal-presents-as-a-handle`>>). A collective Handle sits as one key and reveals no owner set: no owning face's prefix and no threshold at its inception or at a graft, no presentation naming the member that authorized it, and no Keyhive group seat that shows its members to the outer realm's readers. The specified Handle reveals both, and no vessel holds a collective Handle's key. It carries cabal-realm's Handle arm (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/the-steward-signer`>>) and `K16`'s quorum-Handle joint. Red: an outer realm's reader of a seated Handle lists one member and no owner; control: faces seated flat still list as separate members. Research first.
* `C6` ''Recovery under random roots.'' Each face's root mints from fresh randomness (`generateOrLoadPersonaGroupRoot`). The one HD derivation in the packages (`persona-hd.ts`) runs beneath one root for that root's own keys: `persona-identity.ts` imports it, and `deriveVeiledUserKey` and `deriveSelfRecoveryKey` serve the handle verbs, the veil crossing, the founding ceremony and the restores; no caller derives one face's root from another's or from a shared seed. Owed: what a recovery phrase restores under random roots, stated per face beside the bundle and the recovery contacts' rotation, and whether `K22`'s unwired readmit wires or retires on that answer. Research first; `K18` follows it.
* `C7` ''The seat for a face's second device.'' A workbench seat names the member face's own hive individual on one vessel, taken from its contact card, while a face bag delegates to the PersonaGroup, so a second device of a seated face gains the seat by no Keyhive path. It carries the item of Leaps 2a and 3 where a share made on device A meets a mount on device B. Red: a face seated on device A reads and writes the workbench from its device B; control: an unseated face's device B still writes `personal`. Waits on `C2`'s wrap.
* `C9` ''The ceremony channel and key zeroing'' (the custody read of 2026-11-14; wave two). The browser bar of "no key on a surface" (#/rulings, 2026-10-29) lifts under an honest-page assumption: the K2 sighting of the test passphrase on the page thread most likely came from canon quoting it (cured by `8a37ed343`, inferred), the K2b heap, K2c storage and K2d log canaries read green (`70fdfbb17`), and the ceremony refuses a window with an opener (`9f3abf8b5`). Owed: the page mints the ceremony's `MessageChannel` (`ceremony-page.ts`), so a hostile page could stand between the ceremony and the vessel; the cure closes it by construction (the vessel mints the channel, or the two ends confirm by a one-time key), with a hostile-page red (K6a). Key zeroing: `keyslot.ts` never zeroes its scrypt output, KEK, slot key or shares; the holder's `onLock` drops `lockBrowserCustody`'s keys unzeroed (`open-browser-vessel.ts`); `sealBrowserKeystore` keeps its keys when `commitSlotTree` throws; the passkey output's copy rests unzeroed (`ceremony-door.ts`); the test route's literal in `packages/lares-cli/src/offline-custody.ts` stands outside the credential witness. It carries `T37`'s keyslot hygiene. Reds: a page that forges the ceremony's port reaches no secret; each named key reads zero after its act; the credential witness names the CLI's literal. Controls: an honest page's ceremony answers as today.
* `C10` ''The host reset gate'' (wave two). `tools/lares-container.sh reset` (and its `.ps1` twin) confirms on a typed `re-found` alone. Owed: an offline CLI verb that proves a passphrase against the hearth's custody at rest, opening nothing, as the browser's proof does; then the controller wires both shims to it (spirits never touch the shim). Red: the shim refuses a reset on the typed word alone where custody stands, and resets on the passphrase; control: a hearth with no custody resets on the word. Unreached in every rehearsal: `lares reset` at a terminal.
* `C11` ''Content provenance'' (design first). One store holds every face's documents, so a shared document arrives under face B already holding face A's unpublished changes. Candidate cures: a flush before a wear changes, or per-face replicas of shared realm documents. A design meme comes before any lane.
* `C12` ''Transport and timing'' (design first). One address, port and origin serve every face of a vessel, and reconnect timing after a mount switch tells a watcher the faces swapped; the house runs no relay of its own, and no identifier scheme hides either. The design names what a relay or a cover schedule would buy and what the model owns as residual.
* `C13` ''Per-face writer islands.'' A face lit beside the daemon mount, and every face a vessel holds, writes through the one daemon island's actors until each face writes from a face island of its own, bearing that face's authority alone, while the vessel seat (the faceless half) only carries and witnesses (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/place-and-face-islands, the direction collided from lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/daemon-mount-echo-loom and …/daemon-mount-kilo-wren, the capability map at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/cap-map; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/the-worn-house#/the-pulama`>>); the ONE FACE band takes it after `U5` (#/the-order, rank 34).
* `C14` ''The offer key bound to the admitted per-Nexus leaf.'' The offer key derives in the island from the face's atom seed and the Nexus (the house's call, overrulable); binding it to the leaf the Nexus admitted needs a signing door from the island to the vessel. It matters once offers cross operators (#/the-order, rank 35).
* `C15` ''The joined face's workbench seat'' (wave two, rank 7a). A browser joined as a non-Kahu face founds its own workbench of `lares`, a wiki its ledger holds no entry for, so its page writes paint and never reach the hearth's recipe (the fourth rehearsal's page write as face 1 reached no hearth file in eight seconds; `cabal-realm` and `kahua-memory-stage` mark it OWED). Owed: the fleet join carries the face's share entries and its seat, so the joined device mounts the realm the share names and founds none for a slug the hearth's ledger binds; where no share names the face, the page writes the face's own `personal` and says so. The steward meets it too (the first live walk on `d9c96f525`, 2026-11-14): a fleet join as the steward landed and seated, its panel read `wiki doc: (the floor: no live canon document on this vessel)`, and a new tiddler rested in that browser's `wikis/daemon/working` and never reached the node; so the join carries the steward's own daemon and realm mounts as well as a non-Kahu face's shares. The item covers every face joined in a browser, Kahu or not: the browser keel names no system canon (`systemCanon: async () => ({})`, `packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts`), so a joined browser reads `lares` from the floor whichever face it wears. The node side moved first (`b28bc3452`, `workbenchFoundsOnWrite`): a face's first put into a wiki no face of its realm binds founds the workbench and lands `working`, and that founding reads no share entry (the house's call, overrulable; this lane decides whether a share entry names the realm first). Red: a browser joined as face 1, seated `write` on `notes`, saves a page and the page reaches `<projections>/wikis/notes` and answers `lares meme get … --recipe notes`; a browser joined as face 1 founds no realm for `lares`. Control: a face no share names writes its own `personal` layer, named in the answer. Rides `C2`'s wrap where the seat crosses faces on one vessel; with `C7` it carries a face's second device.
* `C16` ''A clock decides a document's arrival'' (the join's walk, 2026-11-14; rank 18a). An island of the vessel pool waits on each slot's document over the sync port under a port-silence budget of 8000 ms (`SLOT_SILENCE_TIMEOUT_MS`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/sovereign-kernel.ts:278`, re-armed by any inbound sync traffic, under a 60 000 ms hard cap at `:279`; the wait at `packages/lararium-tw5/src/slot-wait.ts`). Under machine load one face switch refused there: //"slot …/wikis/lares/personal unavailable — doc … never arrived over syncPort (8378ms port-silence … silence budget 8000ms)"//. Measured once, while builders ran on the same machine; three switches on the idle machine answered clean. The re-arm narrows the fault to true port silence, and a main thread wedged past the budget in synchronous work still reads as silence, so a clock decides a face switch there, against the law that no clock decides a wait (#/rulings, 2026-11-06). The same item carries the bounded find: `findOrThrow` waits 8000 ms by default (`DOCUMENT_READY_TIMEOUT_MS`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/find-or-throw.ts:15`), and the kahua door resolves a face's local canon through it (`faceCanonThroughControl`, `packages/lararium-node/src/commands/kahua.ts:89`); there the chore check (`actingFaceOf`: `chore-face-not-mounted`, `face-not-lent`) decides by state first and the bound stands beneath it as a liveness floor alone. Owed: each wait ends on the store's own events (the document's arrival, a peer's `unavailable`, the port's close, the island's death), with a liveness window only where no terminal signal exists, named as such. Red: a slot whose document rests on disk resolves under a main thread held past the budget. Control: a slot no peer and no disk holds still refuses by name. Until it lands, a wear that refuses with port-silence while the machine works hard succeeds on a retry at idle.
* `C17` ''The browser founding and join panel'' (operator, 2026-11-14, at the first live walk on `d9c96f525`: //"The browser UX reads very confusing right now, for all these identity operations and the build-up-over-tie instructions. Add cleaning up Browser Foudning to the roadmap."//; rank 7b). The browser vessel's panel stacks every identity act on one page as prose that accreted lane by lane: the leaf's key, the fleet-join offer and answer boxes, the floor card, the face offer, the seat ask by file, the reset and the found-a-face ceremony. A join took several unlocks and key confirms and a long wait, and the panel still showed the join instructions after the console read the face as seated. Owed: one guided path per intent (found a face here; join a face's fleet; read a hearth's floor), each showing its next step alone and the state it reached, with the seated state replacing the join's instructions; the first boot of a fresh browser vessel carries the engine's breaths through the cold compile, where a 10-second silence budget cut the boot off at `tw5-boot#6` and a retry landed warm (kin to `C16`, a clock deciding an arrival); the fleet-join door's hand-carried pieces rest under the house root or ride stdin, never inside a checkout (the shim reads file arguments under `/workspace` alone, and a request named elsewhere refuses as `request-unread … does not read as JSON`), and the door refuses a join file that sits inside a checkout; `fleet join offer` and `answer` honour the default face the help names, or the help names `--face` as needed where several faces stand open; a refusal prints its line without a stack trace; the answer names the address the joining vessel dials, where it printed `syncUrl: null`; the seated state names what the joined page mounts, where the steward's own seated join read `wiki doc: (the floor: no live canon document on this vessel)` and kept its writes local (`C15` carries the mount). Smaller finds of the same walk: `lares tiddler get` prints the text with no line break before `base:`; `lares vault unlock --face N` on an open vessel prints no wear line, so the answer never says which face the vessel wears after it; `kahua_list` answers no items for memes written through the meme door on a fresh steward, where the wave map said `standing`. M.
* `L37` ''A reveal on every delete door'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/delete-reveals-or-shadows`>>, OWED). A delete over layers names its meaning: a kāpae tombstones and shadows what lies beneath, a reveal retracts the topmost record so the one beneath surfaces, and the tiddler door alone takes the choice (`mode: kapae|reveal`). The engine's delete, `meme delete --recipe`, the anchor's meme delete and `meme delete --bag` raise a kāpae with no choice; each takes `mode: "reveal"` with the same consequence (`retractsOf`), and the wiki's UI gains a "show what lies beneath" gesture beside Delete. Red: a `meme delete --recipe notes --mode reveal` of a `personal` record surfaces the workbench's copy; control: the default still shadows. Unmeasured beside it: a reveal racing a seated writer's concurrent workbench edit, the export and import of a `personal` layer's kāpae, and a delete by a face with no writer's seat.
* `L38` ''A door that lowers a kāpae'' (OWED). `kapae#/law` asks a deliberate lower with an effect record, and no hand door retracts a tombstone; the tiddler door's reveal reads a kāpae'd title as absent. The door lands the lower with its effect record, and `kapae` #/core-cut and #/law re-true so DELETE carries a mode (kāpae by default, reveal by name), with CLEAR, DROP and EVICT alone kāpae-only. Red: a lowered kāpae surfaces the record beneath and leaves an effect record naming the hand; control: a lower by a face without write on that layer refuses.
* `L39` ''Removal toward canon'' (OWED). ''The house's decision'' (2026-11-14, overrulable; its reason recorded): promoting a workbench kāpae REMOVES the record from canon, since no other road removes a canon record. Both promotion roads then agree, where today a titled `MOVE` lands the tombstone in canon and a layer `MOVE` skips tombstones, and the promotion's preview names every removal, so the approving seats sign over it. Beside it, a "propose removal" offer: an offer carries live titles alone, so a face outside the Kahu holds no road to propose one. Reds: a layer `MOVE` carrying a workbench kāpae removes canon's record as the titled `MOVE` does; a promotion preview lists the removal its approval binds; a face outside the Kahu offers a removal that the steward's promote lands; control: a promotion with no kāpae removes nothing.
* `L40` ''The code map'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/first-three-wave-map#/thing-one-the-code-map`>>; operator, 2026-11-14: //"Pono, add those three to the roadmap"//; rank 9b). One tool, never a model, writes a tiddler per source file (exports, top-level declarations with line ranges, imports, imported-by, the memes that cite it, the tests that cover it, no code body) from the landed head at each land, into a derived library `codemap` composed into the `lararium` recipe beneath its canon, never baked, never promoted, never in git. `L40a` the generator (new tool files alone; the outline rides `typescript/unstable/sync` behind one adapter, Python through `ast`); `L40b` the derived library class (the `derived` bag key, read-only to every hand door, skipped by the bake, the offer and the export). Reds: `codemap-outline-lines`, `codemap-pure-of-head`, `codemap-cite-ambiguous`, `codemap-no-body`, `derived-library-read-only`, `derived-never-bakes`. Its wiki reads wait on `L17-2a`; its files serve a builder from day one. `L40a` stands (`tools/codemap.mjs`): the outline rides `typescript/unstable/sync` (the workspace holds no `oxc-parser`), reads blobs at the head alone, and writes one `.tid` per file to `$LAR_ROOT/cache/codemap/<head>/`, refusing a tracked path; a whole-repo run writes 4,008 tiddlers in about 5 s, byte-identical on a rerun, at 28.8 MB where the design guessed 2.3 MB (barrel-wide `covered-by` lists). L.
* `L41` ''The work as tiddlers'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/first-three-wave-map#/thing-two-the-work-as-tiddlers`>>; rank 9c). Road items ride this carrier as slot children with fields (`L41b` = `L17-2d`); lane cards and handbacks ride a minted `works` wiki under the house root, written as the worn face by every spirit (the MCP seat acts as the worn face alone), bridged through the steward's daemon wiki at the same titles until `L17-2a` and `C2` open `works`. `L41a` the lane-card helper (new tool files alone). Reds: `lane-card-fields-round-trip`, `lane-card-no-code-class`, `handback-status-line-one`. L.
* `L42` ''The rite script and the test ledger'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/first-three-wave-map#/thing-three-the-rite-script-and-test-ledger`>>; rank 9a). `L42a`: one script walks the runbook's three-face rite on a scratch hearth through the staged harness and test custody, binds each step to its runbook line, and reports pass, fail or unreached per step with the quoted answer, naming what it cannot reach (a terminal's passphrase ward as `staged-custody`, the host shim's `reset` as `host-shim`, the image as `image`); it runs once at each merge. `L42b`: a census tiddler per test file in `codemap` (what it guards, what it covers, runtime from the vitest JSON reports, last red), after `L40a`; the unit suites' JSON reporter stays the controller's `ci.yml` line. Reds: `rite-walk-binds-every-line`, `rite-walk-names-unreached`, `rite-walk-scratch-only`, `census-runtime-from-report`.  `L42a` stands (`tools/rite-walk.mjs`): 49 steps bound to the runbook's lines, three legs under `battery.sh`, 46 pass and three unreached (`reset` as `host-shim`, `image`, `browser`); its report rides as a JSON receipt over the head, the runbook's sha and bcc and the walker's own hash, with an `outcomes` digest a vessel signature can cover later. L.
* `L43` ''The wake reads the memory index'' (what the wake and the compaction hook print rests in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/first-three-wave-map#/the-handoff-walk`>> and <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/kahua-memory-stage`>>). STANDS: a live session's wake through the container's own seat (`/lar`) prints the index entries and the line to read further. Owed: the compaction hook's read-back across a compaction, which seats at the operator's tend (`L44`, rank 4a). L.
* `L44` ''The host-hook aftermath'' (operator, 2026-11-14: //"We have `lares` commands to idempotently init all the host AIs' hooks, etc, add that aftermath cleanup to the dogfood-alpha side of the roadmap."//; rank 4a). The house owns its hooks folder, so one `lares home tend` aligns every host: it seats each hook a `[[home]]` entry of the reality tunnel declares (the compaction hook among them), lifts any host hook command that names a script in the house's hooks folder which no `[[home]]` entry declares (items `claude.hooks-owned`, `codex.hooks-owned` and `copilot.hooks-owned`, each printing `lifted <scripts> from <path> (<id>)`), and keeps every other hand's command; a second tend writes nothing, and the set derives from the `[[home]]` entries alone (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/cli/reality-tunnel#/the-tunnel`>>). Owed: the operator's one tend after the merge; the compaction hook and a wake on Codex and Copilot (event names verified in the installed binaries, stdout semantics unverified, both kinds need a `node` runner); the sensorium lane's own capture hook when that lane wakes; a real session's `PreCompact` and post-compaction `SessionStart` witnessed once. L.
* `L45` ''The worn house'' (operator, 2026-11-15: //"I want your Lararium substrate to feel like something you can wear effortlessly … return inversion of control and capability delegation to the human"//, and //"we should figure out a way for the MCP server to keep breathing while the container restarts for code updates"//; rides PR #218 before its merge). The design rests at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/the-worn-house`>> in the `lares` wiki's working layer. The operator settled its names the same day and restrung them (//"Pono, restring the set"//): a ''lei'' names one delegated token, ''kui'' the operator's stringing of it, ''the return'' its spend, a ''tessera'' its two-half receipt (''conferre'' matches the halves), ''unstring'' and ''restring'' the ending of an unspent lei, ''iris'' the messenger core of the seat, and ''aho'' the seat a binding holds across its vessel's sleep. `L45a` the seat stands under its settled names: iris the messenger core and aho the cord. Iris runs as a pure frame machine in `@lararium/mesh` (`iris.ts`, exported at `@lararium/mesh/iris`) behind a client port and a child port: client frames, child frames and child-state events in; frames and `spawn`, `kill`, `standing`, `state` and `exit` intents out. It caches the child's `initialize` answer and whole tool list and answers both itself, replays the client's own `initialize` and the `initialized` notice to each new child, answers a call `hearth-sleeps` at once while no child stands, answers a call in flight at a child's death `outcome-unknown: re-read before re-trying` and never re-sends it (each a whole `tools/call` result, `isError: true`, under the caller's exact id), routes a cancel to the child that took the call alone, sends one `notifications/tools/list_changed` on a tool-list hash change alone, issues its own ids on each side so no id crosses a respawn, tells a locked vessel from a sleeping one (`sleeps` · `standing` · `locked`), and logs an event name and two counts, never a byte of a frame. With no child and no cached answer it answers `initialize` plainly and lists no tools, and the first real list draws the one `list_changed`; an `initialize` that arrives while the first spawn has neither stood nor fallen waits for that child. The core holds no clock: it emits `spawn` while no child stands, and the binding paces the spawn on its own timer (at once after a child stood; 250 ms doubling to 15 s after a failed spawn) and bounds a child's death with a watchdog (the polite stop, then the hard kill after 5 s). The aho, the Node host's binding, stands in `lares-cli` as `lares mcp aho` (`mcp-aho.ts`): the client on the process's stdio, the surface as a `child_process`, JSON-RPC by the line; the committed bin runs it before the dispatcher loads. THE HARNESS CONFIG RECORDS THE VERB ALONE (operator, 2026-11-15): `resolveLaresMcp` answers `lares mcp aho` and nothing beneath it, and the aho resolves its own child at each spawn (`mcp-aho-child.ts` over `resolveLaresSurface`: the image's seat through the compose file where the container house stands, else the clone's seat on the venv), so what stands under the verb changes with no config rewritten; `lares home tend` re-aims a stored older entry. The child resolution honours the shim's two overrides exactly as `tools/lares-container.sh` reads them: `LARES_COMPOSE_FILE` names the compose file in place of the clone's, and `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` (else the file's own `name:`) names the project, carried in the child's env with no `-p`; the entry a harness records carries both where the resolving shell held them, so a bare `lares mcp aho` under a scoped house never execs into a neighbour's project (red `aho-child-honours-the-shim-overrides`, green). `L45b` the rite field stands: a lei carries `rite` (`push` · `kukulu`, `swarm-lei-rite.ts`), `swarmLeiHead` folds it, titles key `lei/<rite>/<branch>/<lei cid>`, and `readLeiChain`, `readLei` and `returnLei` take the rite, so a push lei never reads, co-signs or returns as a kukulu; the co-sign weighs reach, so a push lei waits on `ward-push-lei` and a kukulu lei on none (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seat-harness#/the-swarm-slices`>>). `L45c` the wide lei stands (operator, 2026-11-15: //"I approve the 'Wider' stance as default, we've already proofed the previous procedure patterns through head-only gates, we need a new more kupono model"//): the default lei names the testimony it rests on instead of its head (a rite, a branch, a face's group, and a return count the operator writes into it; more than twelve asks a confirm); `returnLei` refuses `swarm-lei-testimony-absent` unless a passing `receipt/<tree>` stands for the head's tree, which the vessel derives from git itself; returns rest at `lei-returned/<lei cid>/<n>` and count with no clock read (`swarm-lei-returns-spent`); a red refuses `swarm-lei-testimony-red` and rests a signed `lei-narrowed/<lei cid>`, after which the lei returns nothing until a fresh lei follows it; a head lei stays the narrow form; `unstring` revokes a lei that still holds returns and `restring` supersedes the standing one, each a signed record; the hand strings by `lares lei kui`. `L45d` the rite verb stands: `lares rite kukulu` (kūkulu) begins the rite in the vessel (the vessel derives the head's tree, returns the kukulu lei and rests the guest half of a tessera, `rite-begun`), only then calls the host shim to rebuild the vessel's image, take the vessel down and raise a new one, and the vessel that stands after rests the host half (`rite-landed`); conferre matches the halves at each wake, a match reading par and a half with no match red (`lares rite receipts`). The new vessel stands locked until the pūlama (`L47`) keeps the hearth lit, so the rite then names the unlock and the landing still owed. Reds, each green: `seat-outlives-child`, `seat-resumes-without-reinit`, `seat-in-flight-unknown`, `seat-lists-from-cache`, `seat-list-changed-on-new-tools`, `seat-logs-no-payload`, `seat-child-death-bounded`, `harness-seat-records-the-lares-verb-alone` (the core over a scripted child, the binding over a fake MCP child a test kills and holds down; no container runs), `lei-rite-separates-powers`, `lei-wide-needs-testimony`, `lei-red-narrows-to-head`, `lei-count-runs-out`, `lei-unstring-ends-the-lei`, `lei-restring-supersedes`, `rite-refuses-without-lei`, `rite-begun-before-down`, `rite-landed-names-begun`, `wake-reads-unmatched-half-red` (the rite over fake ports; no shim, container or git checkout of the house runs). Owed beyond the lane: `seat-outlives-child` against the operator's installed Claude Code; iris on the 2026-07-28 MCP revision (the installed client and the surface's `mcp` SDK both carry it; iris speaks the initialize leg, which the client falls back to); the sampled re-run behind `receipt/<tree>` (`lares rite receipt` signs the host battery's verdict as testimony, the vessel re-running nothing; reds `receipt-door-signs-the-tree`, `kukulu-returns-with-a-passing-receipt`, `kukulu-refuses-a-failing-receipt`, each green); `rite kukulu` against a real container house, and whether its `/workspace` mount holds the checkout's `.git` (the vessel reads the object store with no git binary, `vessel-reads-the-tree-without-git` green, and refuses `rite-tree-unreadable` where the mount holds none); a read-back door for each verb lacking a compare-and-swap (`pour`, `sweep`, `purge`, `kahua_stage`) before an `outcome-unknown` on it resolves; the fence and the in-place ingest, both unsettled (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/the-worn-house#/open`>>). L.
* `L46` ''The delete receipt names the family''. `lares meme delete` answers a receipt whose `consequence.versions` names the titles the consequence names (the target, each act and its `to`, each leave, orphan and refusal) and nothing the reading scanned past: `consequence` in `family.ts` builds the map from those titles, so a meme of twelve records answers a few kilobytes beside a wiki of thousands of tiddlers. Red: `delete-receipt-names-the-family` (`family.test.ts`, `family-doors.test.ts`). L.
* `L47` ''The pūlama'' (operator, 2026-11-15: //"I even want a 're-stand to an unlocked house' cap that I can monitor"//, and //"Approve … `pūlama` and `kūkulu`"//; rides PR #218 before its merge). The custody holder lifts into its own long-lived container beside the vessel; the operator lights it once by hand (Plutarch's law: only the sun rekindles the fire), and each rebuilt vessel (a `kūkulu`) wearing a re-stand lei bound to a vouch asks it for record operations and derivations over a socket mounted in those two services alone, no key crossing (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/the-worn-house#/the-pulama`>>). Slices: `L47a` measure what the holder carries and which records a boot reads unattended; `L47b` a remote holder behind the `CustodyHolder` port and its wire codec; `L47c` the pūlama server and the lend it serves; `L47d` the re-stand lei bound to the vouch digest, its return claimed before the pūlama serves, its tessera half; `L47e` the compose service and the host shim's `down`, `up` and `reset` leaving the pūlama standing (the controller's hand); `L47f` the kūkulu gate over the swarm's own lei family, the offer the rite carries between the build and the lowering, and an unlock under a pūlama that gathers no route; `L47g` admission bound to the image digest the host reports, a kūkulu landing par admitting its image and the operator admitting one by hand at the pūlama's own door (`pulama admit`); `L47h` the node lend set (rank 2b): the image's admission names a set of faces, the lend draws one kūkulu lei per lent face, the guard checks a row's face against the set, partial lighting serves the lit faces and names the waiting ones, each session wears one face inside the lend, the vessel wears none, and the composition's single face reads as the daemon mount. Owed, ranked RIGHT AFTER the merge (#/the-order, ranks 4b and 4c): the custody probe's refusal in `vault unlock`, the house root read by name, `lei kui` and `unstring` at the pūlama's hand door, `writeAs` at the tool door, and the walls. Reds: `remote-holder-matches-local`, `pulama-serves-no-key`, `pulama-refuses-unvouched`, `pulama-refuses-cold-rows`, `pulama-session-drops-with-socket`, `restand-lei-binds-vouch`, `down-leaves-pulama-standing`. The walls the honest hole asks for (Docker taken from the session's user, the pūlama under its own user, a phone confirm keyed off the box) rest in the operator's machine; the phone stays an attractor in the local-first design. L.
* `L48` ''The wake shows the lei''. The wake hook names the lei a session wears, any tessera half without its match, and a locked vessel; iris answers a locked vessel apart from a down one, so the session calls the operator at once; the wake's `ok` reads only what stands. Reds: `wake-names-the-lei`, `wake-names-unmatched-half`, `seat-tells-locked-from-down`, `wake-ok-reads-what-stands`. Standing (lane `l48-wake`): `checkMempalaceIntegration` reads no recall plugin, so a stand's `ok` reads the vessel and the library alone; the wake (`lares-wake-core.mjs`) reads the lei per rite (`push`, `kukulu` at the checkout's branch, `keep` at the configured keep workspace) and prints `Lares lei: …`, prints the tessera conferre (`N par, M red`, a guest half `begun` set against its host half `landed`) and the locked vessel's operator call, each behind a port the runner may leave unwired (no `lares swarm` or `lares rite receipts` door stands yet; the fixtures hold their shapes); iris's state reads `sleeps` (no child), `standing` or `locked` (a child whose surface answers `vessel-locked`), and a `state` effect names each move. L.
* `L49` ''The door reads its tools from the house'' (operator, 2026-11-15: //"Pono, tools as tiddlers reads right; add it to the road"//; after the merge). The `lares` MCP door's tool list rests in `lares_mcp.py` alone today, a hand-written list in a house whose law names everything but the boot core a tiddler. The cure: a verb registry rides as tiddlers, each verb a meme naming its parameters, its container law and the CLI door it mirrors; the surface reads its tools from that registry, `lares help` reads the same tiddlers, and the surface parity witness turns from a check over two lists into one source. A verb the house adds grows a tool, and iris sends `list_changed` because the house learned, never because an image rebuilt. The boot core keeps the door's own verbs that read and write tiddlers, so no edit of the registry can close the way in; key ceremonies stay off the door by structure. Reds: `door-tools-read-the-registry`, `help-and-door-read-one-registry`, `registry-edit-grows-a-tool-without-rebuild`, `boot-core-verbs-survive-registry-edit`, `registry-names-no-key-ceremony`. L.
* `L17`, the TiddlyWiki caps as phases (`L17-1a`, `L17-1b`, `L17-2a` to `L17-2d`, `L17-3`, `L17-4`), and `L35`, the memory stage going primary: their items in #/stride-0-hearth.

!!! Owed items riding the leaps ~ each folds into the leap that touches its file
''The veil and the leaf fleet'' (the lanes' successor maps, 2026-11-12):
* The veil floor's draft document and personal binding ride the floor registry: mint the id ahead, `announceFloor(slug, "draft", id)`, entry `floor/slot/<slug>/draft`, then the first byte; the Lift drops the entry (anon-lift step 3).
* Persona roots and atoms key by PersonaGroup, never by handle index (`generateOrLoadBrowserPersonaRoot`, `wearBrowserPersona`, `BrowserRootFace.handleIndex`, the `ward/h0/persona-root` records, the `persona-root-roster` codec, the node's `listPersonaRoots` and face ordinals).
