* A joined node's landing and its later boots read one island, in two shapes no red covers (Reload-Mender's read of the code, 2026-11-14, unmeasured; the single-face joinee and the browser stand cured, #/ashes `joined-reload`). A face that lands beside a standing one (`packages/lararium-node/src/commands/init.ts`, the `landsBeside` branch) seeds its persona-KEL chain on the payload's island (`admittedJoineeIsland(payload)`) while the vessel boots on the island it already stood. A joinee that seats its own charter boots on `ownGenesis` (`nodeNexusStandsAt`, `packages/lararium-node/src/nexus-standing.ts`) while its landing seeded the payload's island. Red for each: the landed face's chain reads on the board the next boot resolves. Control: a single-face joinee with no charter restarts on the island its admit named (`tests/joined-node-restart-island.test.ts`, NR1 to NR3).
* The leaf lean's stale-text sweep: the `hearthTrueName()` accessor in `genesis-artifact.ts` renames to name the engine CID it returns, with its callers; code comments in `device-delegation.ts`, `ceremony-core.ts`, `lar-uris.ts`, `tw5-host-bridge.ts` and `tests/leaf-fleet-admit.test.ts`; canon in lararium-identity #/head, epoch-binding-surfaces, identity-classes #/the-two-relations, kahu, engine-watch, persona-circle and federation. Reds: a gateless joinee's edge reads byte-identical across an engine CID move; a leaf's cabal sentinel seeds from the bare URI; a leaf joinee's face join clears against the root's `""` edge.
* The route door's remainder (#/rulings, 2026-11-12, no query string): the mesh-leaf door, where a leaf's peers enter as a file kind of their own at the page's carriage door, beside the floor card and the anchor (`?mesh=` burned with `?flow=` and `?c4trace`; the vessel hello carries no `meshLeaf`, and no page door hands the vessel a peer list); a composition whose relay origin differs from its web origin (the arrival descriptor names no relay, and the page dials its own origin's); a QR drawn for the banner's floor card. Built: the arrival address names the page alone, its relay comes from the same-origin arrival descriptor, and the floor card and its anchor come in at the page's carriage door.
* Two leaves converge over a road after the seat: a herm in the answer's reach, or a peer road.
* The burn's replica layer: re-seal the face's workbench tiddlers under the vessel key before a clear, and mount the last-read replica read-only beneath the fresh floor layer.
* The mirror census guard: wherever a vessel first answers `sealedRest` true, a veil floor's mirror still runs no person-authored code.
* A lit set wider than one face per boot (`faceProviders.lit` refuses `face-edge-absent` for a second face). The node lend set (`L47h`, rank 2b) meets this ceiling: a lend of three faces asks a composition that stands three, so the lend's vessel lane checks it first.
* A browser wearing a joined face while it holds another face's root lists no root (`browserRootFaces`); the joinee's answer intake holds a paste box alone; `browserSeatDevice`'s set-aside check duplicates the node's `assertDyadBinds`; a QR read on a device carrying a reader, and WebKit, stand unmeasured.

''The leaps of 2026-11-11'' (the controller's list):
* Measure the realm-per-wiki founding cost (every non-daemon wiki stands a realm).
* `createHouseCanon` cleared at the gate with no `kahuReach` source reads even the steward as a stranger; sibling slot resolvers write binding records into the worn face's daemon store; a real two-face boot proves the sibling label path; source comments still say "system canon"; the CHANGELOG owes a line for `LitFaceSlotSpec.atomKey`.
* The face-intent door's timing flake (await the detach, never a clock); `found` ends a beat late until Enter; a re-run `up` after an interrupted one errored (capture at the next sighting).
* `canonicalCarrierForm` in the override base re-implements TW5's `.tid` serialization: one algorithm, one authority.
* Leap 0's tail (the epoch burn, #/the-order rank 18): the persona KEL's readers (`persona-kel-board`, `face-bundle-restore`, `face-provisional`, `persona-kel-ring`, `sibling-channel`), face-authority's `position`, the edge frontier and the journals order by hash-chain descent with `seq` as a cross-check alone; the web's genesis anchor and live status read the seed format through `wire-names`; the Python sensorium's trial tags weigh apart (they may key stored trial data).
* Leaps 2a and 3: between a replica ingesting a Keyhive revoke and its next roster read, the old seat record stands (re-project on every ingest, or route the guard into the island). The device-A share meeting a device-B mount rides `C7`.
* Leap 4: offers from another vessel never reach the steward's replica (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/offering`>>); a retire counts any seat of the charter it names, where a seat a later roll removed could still retire, closed by reading the charter head; a promotion asks the charter seat before canon moves and lands and retires as one outcome, so only a retire that fails past that check leaves its offer open until a replay retires it; the browser offering page and Kahu board, offering a removal, the steward's decline and `offer list` paging; a seatless `offer-retire-unseated`, unreached in every rehearsal.
* Leap 5: the worn face holds per vessel, never per session; the unsigned move into `bags/daemon-<F>` stays unproven by a run; a code sweep of the CLI help's "strictly higher version" and of comments saying the address secret derives working documents. The bag shares' own resolver stands owed at #/rulings (2026-11-11).
* The pre-walk lane: the test-typecheck ratchet burns down (ceilings only fall); a browser face label rests in OPFS and dies with site data, and no browser door reads labels; a batch lift naming staged memes (`L21`; the MCP seat stages through `kahua_stage` and proposes through `kahua_propose`); the binding answer carries the whole workbench snapshot on every faced mount (trim to create-time or changes since heads).
* The witness fleet: `ahu-pair-parity` needs the tree-sitter wasm on the host; `browser-weld-witness` C4.2's reload flaked three times on a cold dev cache, unproven. The S3 stage walk's relay race, partly cured by `16e64ad89`, reads green since.
* The mirror's items rest in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/d3-glass-lane#/owed`>>, the vessel floor's in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane#/owed`>>.

''The rite's ledger and the day's handbacks'' (2026-11-13):
* The confirm gate rides `C4`, the shared Kahu-cabal workbench for house-canon wikis rides `P21` (#/the-leaps, the leaps of 2026-11-14).
* ''A draft's recovery mirror rests in the writing face's root'' (face-pools lane P1, 2026-11-18): each face's unsaved drafts of a shared wiki rest at `<projections>/faces/<pet name>/recovery/<slug>` (its temp beside, at `temp/<slug>`), never under the shared `wikis/<slug>/`, and the export carries them for that face alone.
* ''The fifth rehearsal's residue'' (2026-11-14): an export names no omission where a shared workbench's folder carries zero pages (a reader's hold alone wakes no working mirror; the runbook's carry block holds as a seated writer first); the final seed's zero line; the handoff walk's `kahua_list` read per face; a wrong passphrase at the browser reset shows no error line (`C4`); `--base ""`.
* ''A contract-tier bag never rides the public floor.'' The public floor every DreamNet user reads by CID carries `public`-tier bags alone, read off each bag's own `meta.mem` at the genesis bake and at each release cut (a bag that declares no tier reads `veil` and stays off); the contract-tier `bags/elyncia-referee` keys no snapshot, and a hearth founded earlier sheds its referee snapshot at its next `lares nexus release <file> --cut`, the slug named in `dropped`. Owed under that law: the referee recipe that mounts `elyncia-referee` for a contracted seat.
* ''One resolver answers house canon.'' `resolveHouseCanon` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/house-canon-doc.ts`) answers every door that reaches house canon: the Kahu realm's standing document first (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/offering#/the-canon-offer`>>), a registry entry only where the realm names none. A house-canon wiki the realm names no document for mints none, files no catalog entry and keys its slot bindings on `floorCanonAddress` (`floor:<bag>`). Owed: burning a stale `bags/lares` catalog entry an earlier boot filed.
* ''The console door's remainder'' (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/browser-vessel-lift#/the-console-door`>>): a verb plane, where each verb declares a `console` surface and the door projects the daemon's reads by that declaration; `vault lock` house-wide (the browser refuses it `locks-by-leaving`, and a lock that closes every tab's session needs a locked state on the page and a road to unlock on a standing connection); the build revision read off the arrival descriptor into `vessel read`.
* ''A crossing leaves no log line at the face gate'' (`face-gate-server.ts` writes none): one line per admitted and per refused crossing, naming the face and no key material; the wire's own silence stays (#/decisions, silence, one deadline).

''Items with wake conditions'': the herm-never-unlocks refusal, before a herm stands for real; the signed local channel (`F11`) covering `meme_put`, before a second human, a remote seat or a non-operator process writes the hearth; the parallel-drafts door, when a second place joins a face; `lares vessel read --control` (a read-only, redacted view of control records), the daemon document's vessel state moving into the control document, and a page-dispatched verb's answer travelling back to its page island.

''After the walk'' (#/the-order ranks each): the Mu on the two floor confirmations (#/rulings, 2026-11-10; rank 28); the control-plane leap, `bags/daemon` moving to the vessel's control home (rank 34); the branch burn by reachability from `main`, the race sampler branches among them (rank 38); the complete re-think of the multi-model and swarm procedures once the Lararium fully stands (#/rulings, 2026-11-13; rank 31). The AI's memory frame and the kahua two-tier lift ride `L35`; `M5`'s memory migration, rulings and feedback first, rides rank 4; the span's pull request to `main`, then `develop`, rides rank 2.

