!! Stride 0 Hearth

The memory-stage hearth (#/the-attractor; #/rulings, 2026-10-31): the joined walk first, then the stage on it, then the move. Each item runs red-first with its control; an item's harness half walks the test door, and the operator's hand performs each founding and custody act (#/cold-start).

''Reading note'': the tree and git decide what stands (#/the-loops). Each item names the shape the tree holds today and what stays owed on it; landed work reads in git and #/ashes.

!!! Seven-league stride notes

* ''The stage's shape''. The stage rests in the face's own daemon wiki and climbs by two crossings: the working top, where a stage meme stands under `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/<class>/<slug>`, its path carried by title and `uri-path`; the face's local canon `bags/daemon-<F>`, unsigned, by `lares kahua stage`; and the signed stage `bags/kahua-<F>`, by the hand's lift (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/kahua-memory-stage#/as-built`>>). Stage memes stay out of git (#/rulings, the memory stage's meme path). The stage scout's lean (two rounds, 2026-10-31) stays a lean the controller rules through `L8`: a `stage/*` tag family beside `lifecycle/*`, so an unpoured meme never enters the governed count and a meme poured as a carrier takes `lifecycle/*` at the pour; one index view; survivors reaching `bags/` carriers by promotion; consolidation through a sitting, and through a talk-story floor where a stage meme contradicts held canon; no stage meme reads a clock.
* ''Where the operator's hearth stands'': the house as a container puts all code in the image (#/rulings), and `tools/lares-container.sh` stands it on the one house root `LARES_HOUSE` names, bound at `/lar`.
* ''The operator's hand on the hearth'', each when its item stands: move the old homes aside and found fresh by hand (#/fresh-start; #/rulings, 2026-10-31, a single operator's re-found); unlock; bind the browser's passphrase slot; carry the fleet-join offer, request, answer and land; run `lares home tend` from the main clone. None of these gates a lane.

!!! The items

* `F11` The hands: the watcher as a leasing session, the seat under a standing grant, the Mask as a record field, door parity at the session (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands`>>). An agent's dissent drafts and a person's direct ask edits (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). O1. The four profiles stand in the session contract (`HAND_PROFILES`, `session-contract.ts`), and a session seated `seat` refuses the hand-only verbs at the socket by name: the kahua operator verbs `beyond-profile`, the promote and kāpae verbs `promote-needs-hand` and `kapae-needs-hand` (`uds-channel.ts`, `store-door-verbs.ts`). That refusal reads advisory, since a client names its own hand. Owed, before a second human, a remote seat or a non-operator process writes the hearth (#/the-leaps, the items with wake conditions): the signed local channel that binds the hand; the profile-verb table over the vault, admit and face-switch verbs, where `session:call` and `session:act` check the face and the anchor alone; the Mask carried on the seat's `meme_put`; the watcher's lease and door parity behind them.
* `L4p` The stage walk's proof (walk gap G3; `L4` rests in #/ashes). Owed: the walk itself on `tools/browser-weld/`, red then control. A joined browser edits a tiddler in the daemon wiki, the file lands under `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>`, `lares meme get --recipe default` returns it, a CLI `meme put` shows in the page, and the MCP seat reads the page's edit; weakening control: with the relay killed, no file lands. It reads rung 2 whole (#/the-road, the shore). Waits on a stood hearth and on `L4f`. L; B.
* `L4f` `L4`'s fork (a) (operator ruling, 2026-11-04; ruled, unbuilt). The admit carriage widens so the operator's own-hearth page mounts the hearth daemon document, where today an own-hearth crossing seats the hearth's canon documents alone (`hearth-canon.ts`, `seatHearthCanon`). Red: a joined own-hearth page mounts the daemon wiki through the widened carriage and edits land under `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>`; control: a guest page's admit carries no daemon document. Sighted twice: the fourth rehearsal's page write as face 1 reached no hearth file in eight seconds, and on the live walk of 2026-11-14 a tiddler saved in a joined browser's daemon wiki never reached the node. Rides `L4p`. The slice's design rests in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/kahua-memory-stage#/the-hearth-lane`>>. Stands in code, walked by no live page: the name rides the per-device `device-edge` act as `hearthDaemon`, root-signed at each seat from the hearth's own control record (never `hearthDaemonUrl`, which names the door document); the hearth's vessel-only verdict yields that one working slot to a session that proved its face, and the device table answers the current binding alone (`workingOf`), so a moved slot shares nowhere. Owed: `L4p`'s walk on a fresh `fleet join answer`; a joined device's earlier working slot stays orphaned until a lift. L; B.
* `L8` The memory stage's law. <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/kahua-memory-stage`>> holds the stage as built: it lives in the `daemon` wiki itself (operator ruling, 2026-10-31, #/rulings), its working layer projects to `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>`, the face's daemon canon to `<projections>/bags/daemon-<F>` and the face's kahua stage to `<projections>/bags/kahua-<F>` (`bag-paths.ts`), and no other wiki domain hosts it, since each serves its own intent. Owed in that carrier, as law before `L10` to `L13` build on it: the tiers as tags inside that one wiki (the `stage/*` family beside `lifecycle/*`), how a survivor promotes into a bag carrier, the consolidation rite, the cold-boot index, and the rhymes with the field (complementary learning systems, hippocampal indexing, reconsolidation, the agent-memory systems), each with its source and where it breaks. L.
* `L33` ''The stage-meme gate's residues'' (`L9`'s blind read's P3s). The gate compares raw strings, so `Memory/`, a `%2F` spelling or a title with no trailing slash skips the missing-key check while the stage's readers filter on the exact prefix; a keyed stage meme's `/path` children can sit at another key's derived title; a noop or conflict verdict, and a write that bypasses `placeMeme`, skip the gate (the read-side stage law, `L11`, covers them). `tools/dogfood-proof.sh` unsets `LAR_BAGS` and `LAR_GENESIS` beside its exports, so an operator shell that exports `LAR_BAGS=<checkout>/bags` never writes back into the tracked tree; corepack's `pnpm` under the proof's fresh `HOME` may fetch. L.
* `L34` ''The kāpae on disk's residues'' (lane `kapae-disk`; the seat's decisions, overrulable). The disk watcher sends a `.kapae` shadow the way it sends a carrier, both ends treating a repeat as a no-op; a tombstone raised while the projector stood stopped writes no shadow at boot (a gap older than the lane); a title ingest-back cannot address (a foreign title, a `FileSystemPaths` rule) gets no usable shadow, a named limit. Accepted: a rename re-link retracts its source to absent (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/core-cut`>>), so a lower copy surfaces. L.
* `L10` The lifecycle tools read the stage: `meme check` counts no `stage/*` meme among governed carriers, and `lares meme sitting` names closed stage memes with a landed witness as burn candidates and burns none (`carrier-lifecycle.ts`). Red: a `stage/working` meme with no witness passes `meme check`, and a closed meme with a witness appears in the sitting; control: a `lifecycle/designed` carrier still meets its gate. L.
* `L11` The cold-boot index: one filter view on the daemon wiki lists the open stage memes, each beside the commit or wave that last re-checked it and an `unchecked` mark where none did, and the boot set stays one fixed small read whatever the history holds. Red: a stage meme whose named file moved since its last check reads `unchecked`; control: a re-checked meme reads its stamp. Owed with it (#/rulings, the memory stage's meme path, (a) and (b)): the index and every stage reader read working and canon, never drafts, and a stage meme whose title disagrees with its key reads as a named fork, the backstop writing a diagnostic tiddler in the working bag; the readers read a stage meme through `readParallelDrafts`, so concurrent same-key edits surface both sides before multi-device dogfooding. L.
* `L12` The recurrence loop: an incident record carries `recurs/N`, counted by repeat incidents, never a clock; at two a sitting proposes a procedural change (a feedback line or a guard test, red-first), the operator rules it, and a lesson stays `unverified` until a later incident shows it held, a lesson that never fires reading as a burn candidate. Red: a second incident of one tell raises the proposal; control: one incident raises none. L.
* `L13` The move, the rung's acceptance: the controller's plan, its owed list, the scout reports, the lane briefs and the resume sheets move onto the stage, and a cold session reads the stage index, this carrier and the controller handoff (#/cold-start). Until then the sprint's planning records rest in the repository's `scratch/` directory as history (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history`>>), live plans rest in canon (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff#/state`>>), and the stage holds none of them. The harness's own auto-memory keeps its seat, since its host loads it through its own door; the reality tunnel's memory shore may later point it at the stage (#/side-lanes). Its witness: one cold session resumes the controller's work from the stage alone. L.
* `L14` The promotion verb, landing last: `meme promote` holds no in-wiki path, its admin check answers `false` (`meme.ts`), and the hand-edit weld stays unbuilt (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology`>>). Red: a person holding admin promotes a working-layer meme into a bag as a residency move, its `lar:` URI unchanged; control: a seat's promotion refuses. Until it lands, a stage meme reaches `bags/` as a carrier poured by pull request. L.
* `L15` A live house beside the land train. A house's projection lands under `<LAR_ROOT>/projections`, outside the checkout; the tracked tree takes a house's writes only where its canon source resolves to the checkout's `bags/` (`LAR_BAGS=<checkout>/bags`, source-control write-back by design), and `tools/tree-clean-witness.sh` reads any write a test run adds to the tracked tree as red. Owed for the write-back case, where a dirty tracked file blocks the land train's fast-forward on that path: the house's canon edits commit as their own record commits (or the train reads and carries them) before a land, and the witness reads the house surface apart from a test boot's writes. Red: a standing house edits a canon tiddler, a train lands a commit touching another file, and the land succeeds with the house edit kept. L.
* `L17` The whole TiddlyWiki surface on every door, as phases (operator, 2026-10-31: //"The MCP server should also have full TW5 caps on any wiki loaded."//; a priority lane since 2026-11-14; the lean approved: //"Pono!!! I approve all!"//; shape, reds and files at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-surface-scout#/phases`>>, the door as it stands at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-surface-scout#/what-stands`>>). Base operations stop wearing `meme_*`: "meme" names a family of tiddlers (a root and its slot children), the meme door keeps the family verbs, and every write-bearing action reads meme-aware. Phase 1 stands: one family law with the orphan folder and its flag, and the tiddler door on the anchor, worn by the CLI and the MCP seat, its delete joined to the family law and naming its meaning by `mode` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/delete-reveals-or-shadows`>>). ''Owed in phase 1's wake'': `meme delete` on the anchor lands one change per member and takes no mode (`L37`); a slot's delete leaves its root's `kahea` call dangling (the consequence names it; no door rewrites the root); caps against the family live in the pure function alone; a COPY of a root copies one record; a rename lands as ordered writes, never one change; the wiki's indexes count a hidden record, so a `count[]` over an indexed lookup can tell one exists; a `$:/` write refuses `tiddler-put-code-class` until the act ward's `codeClassOf` stands.
** `L17-2a` (wave two) The relay to named wikis: a width-`none` port under a lease minted from the session's face. Reds: `wiki-filter-named-wiki-engine`, `relay-lease-from-session-face`, `relay-second-face-refuses`. Files: `open-node-vessel.ts`, `vessel-island-pool-core.ts`, `port-lease.ts`; it uses the port's standing kinds.
** `L17-2b` (wave two) The `act` and `catalog` asks, the recorder in a throwaway copy, preview by default and apply by digest, bulk by filter, the empty `tm-*` allowlist; the switcher's rename to `wiki_switch|hold|release|active` rides with `wiki_act`. Reds: `wiki-act-preview-then-apply`, `preview-bound-to-cursor`, `wiki-act-custody-refuses`, `wiki-act-tm-allowlist-empty`, `bulk-act-half-family-refuses`, `cap-family-split-names-layers`. Files: `record-port.ts` (`2b` alone edits it), `record-port-handler.ts`, a new `act-recorder.ts`, `codeClassOf` in mesh.
** `L17-2c` (wave two, after `2b`) The meme door's remainder on `familyOf`: `meme put|get|delete` compose a port write, and a root's rename carries its family as one change. Red: `rename-root-carries-family`. Files: `place-meme.ts`, `meme-verbs.ts`.
** `L17-2d` (wave two) The road's items as slot children carrying fields (`status`, `priority`, `depends-on`, `lane`), so a filter reprioritizes the road; a content lane on this carrier alone, after a ruling on the road's slot law.
** `L17-3` (after wave two) The console verbs (`console-verbs.ts`, `console-door.ts`), the filter and action references as MCP resources, a change feed by filter and `wiki_since`, a cross-wiki search naming each hit's wiki, the AI's own draft slot, new-from-template; DreamDOM's `D19` carries the surface half.
** `L17-4` (later) Signed provenance telling an operator's verbatim ruling from a session's paraphrase (after `F11`'s signed local channel), a family-aware rename with relink across wikis, an L-Prime lint operator.
* `L18` The narration fence: self-narration, design notes, talk-story floors and their moʻolelo and hoike, scout reports, lane briefs, resume sheets, and the controller's plan and owed items land in the daemon wiki through `meme_put`, never as files on disk. The fence rides three hands: the lead law and `mixed-model-swarm` carry the rule; a harness hook refuses a write to the controller's scratch notes and to the flat memory store beyond its pointer file, naming `meme_put` (installed through the operator's own config act); a witness counts stray narration files. Red: an agent's write to the fenced path refuses and names the wiki verb; control: a lane's code edit in its worktree passes. Lands after `L13`. L.
* `L19` The memory o-takiage: the flat memory store moves into the daemon wiki, each file a tiddler keyed by its slug (`stage/feedback`, `stage/semantic`, `stage/reference`, the `[[name]]` links kept as wiki links), checked against the repo as it moves (a memory that names a file, function or flag gets re-verified, and a stale one burns rather than moves); each moved file burns from the flat store; the index file shrinks to a pointer whose first line names the MCP capabilities and the cold-boot filter. Red: a cold session reads a moved memory through `meme_get` and the filter view, with the flat file gone; control: the pointer's first line answers before any wiki stands. Lands after `L18`, and in this shape (talk-story, 2026-11-04): the first copy lands in the kahua working top, titles `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/<class>/<slug>` (the slug holds the filename stem, hyphenated; fields `name`, `description`, `type`, `source-file`, `source-sha256`); dangling links report and stay uninvented; the flat files stay source of truth until each receipt stands; a stale memory burns instead of moving; the pointer file shrinks last. It needs `L4p`'s stage walk and `L17`'s filter verbs first, and `L21` lifts the verified batches by hand. The stage meme law already binds every writer (`stageMemeRefusal`, `place-meme.ts`), and the burn it rests on holds on disk (#/rulings, the memory stage's meme path, (c); `kapae-disk` in #/ashes): the projector writes a burned meme's kāpae as `<stem>.kapae` and ingest raises it again. Owed beside the move: a burn discards or shadows the open drafts and upper-layer copies of its meme, so no synced draft brings a burned memory back. L. Its cold-boot reads ride the tiddler door: `wiki_filter` for the index, `tiddler_get` for one meme.
* `L21` The batch lift (`L19`'s owed half, 2026-11-04). `L19` lands its first copy in the kahua working top, never the daemon wiki, and verifies there (a `meme_get` round-trip against `source-sha256`, a receipt tiddler per file, the filter view, a cold-session sample); the operator's hand then lifts the verified tiddlers in BATCHES, one fresh ward unlock per batch (#/rulings, 2026-11-05), each item still signing its own lift act, all items preflighted before any lands, the epoch pinned once, and a drifted digest refusing by name. Red: a batch of N working-top tiddlers lifts as N signed lifts under one warded hand act, and a tiddler whose digest drifted from its receipt refuses by name; control: a single lift stays as before. Waits on `L4p`, `L17` and the kahua stage. L.
* `L35` ''The memory stage goes primary'' (operator, 2026-11-14). Once the hearth answers, the wiki replaces the flat markdown memory: a face reads its own daemon wiki and every topic wiki shared to it, so the house's shared memory lives in a shared topic wiki and a face's own memory in its daemon wiki; a verbatim search of past chat stays the deferred sensorium's. It builds on `L8`'s law, `L17`'s verbs and `L19`'s move with `L21`'s lift, and closes with `L13`: a rule in the harness's `CLAUDE.md` naming the wiki as the memory, and the burn of the flat files once each receipt stands; the wake's memory index and the compaction hook's carried addresses stand beneath it (`L43`, `L44`). The rule lands through the operator's own config act, as `L18`'s hook does. It carries the AI's memory frame (a memory's structure and provenance as fields, never bare data) and the kahua two-tier lift. Reds: a cold session with the flat store gone reads its memory index at wake and a shared house memory from the topic wiki shared to its face; after a compaction the session reads a meme again by the address the hook carried. Control: a face no share names reads nothing of that topic wiki. Waits on the first use (#/the-order, rank 5). L.
* `L22` The swarm's controls and the ward (operator rulings, 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05; the slices, their state and the design of `S3` to `S6` rest in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seat-harness#/the-swarm-slices`>>). Item 7 of the seat-harness lane enacts the wiki-daemon key cap at standing: the house cap, the lane shares, the push lei, the lane state, the roster and the receipts rest as signed records, the ward binds the daemon and kahua wikis' code-bearing acts and the kahua lift, and the swarm refuses by name before a wiki stands. `S1` to `S3` with `S2b`, `S3-pre-b` and `S3b` stand (#/ashes, the `row7` lines). Owed: `S4` to `S6`, after the standing, red-first per slice, each with its control, homed in the suites the carrier names. The reads' residues ride `L24` to `L27`. L.
* `L24` ''The stuck joinee'' (`S3a`'s cure R1; the house lean the operator approved, 2026-11-05). A seated admission whose device edge lapsed across a lease roll refuses `replay-edge-lapsed`. The renewal writer stands: `packages/lararium-node/src/commands/device-admit.ts` appends one `device-edge` act for the seated admission at the current epoch when the seated digest changes, signed by the face root, and the persona fold takes the later act's digest. Owed: re-measure, never rebuild: which acts roll the delegation lease epoch, whether every joined device strands at such a roll and whether the renewal covers every seated device, read over every lease-advancing act until `M6`'s lease burn retires the roll. Red: a joinee seated before a lease roll rejoins and stands on the operator's answer; control: a replay with no operator answer still refuses. L.
* `L29` ''The teardown drain'' (Terra read, 2026-11-06). The island submits every owed write, then settles in one round on the vessel's close: the vessel answers each receipt whenever asked, the island sends `receipt:asks-done` once every owed write has asked, the vessel answers and sends `receipt:close`; no island-side clock; a title still owed reaches the vessel by name as a `teardown-fault`, never a silent ack. Every vessel class tears its daemon island down before its floor (the herm's order cured; the browser's island takes the graceful shutdown, its hard kill the liveness for a worker wedged alive). Owed: the two ask doors that still end on any fault (fail-safe; narrowing after a measure), a dedicated browser island's owed writes at `pagehide`, a full herm boot teardown proof. L.
* `L30` ''The swarm moves into the Lararium'' (operator, 2026-11-07, #/rulings). After standing and the vault: the multi-model swarm harness now in `tools/` (the broker `commit-relay.mjs` and `seat-broker.mjs`, the walls `seat-walls.mjs`, the launcher `launch-codex.mjs`, the lane state, the push grant, the gate, the land train) moves into the capability stack, each part to the home its nature names: product code, plugin code running inside the VM, or a shore connector at a causal-island boundary; the daemon then drives the swarm from inside the Lararium. Builds on `S4` to `S6` (signed roster, receipts and controls in the daemon wiki) and the vault (`L22`, #/the-order rank 31). Owed after standing.
* `L28` ''The renewal at the roll stands unwired'' (`L24`'s roll half; the unwired-code scout, 2026-11-06). `rollEnrolments` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-group-secret.ts`) seals one enrolment per remaining device at a rotation, and only tests call it; the renewal at the roll, which moves each seated device's pin to a renewed edge the root signed (the lease guard, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seat-harness#/the-swarm-slices`>>), holds no production caller. Owed: a zero-trust critical review decides retire / wire / reshape, then the work (#/rulings, 2026-11-06, the unwired code); the Terra review's verdict sets its next step. Before the rite. L.
* `L32` ''The lease end state's remaining slices'' (merged into the epoch burn, #/the-order rank 18; `M6`; lane `lease-end`, whose slices 1 and 2 stand; after the dogfood stand, operator 2026-11-07). Slices 3 and 4: slice 2's owed items (KEL freshness, the tri-state ring, the founder join's check-then-use window, the post-commit set-aside, the census that refuses an incomplete view, `runApplyAdmitPayload`, `holder-session-proof`, `leaf-peer-proof`), then the roll guard and the epoch burn (#/rulings, the face lease's end state, reshaped). Slice 2's blind read owes its P3s: the commit boundary's wording (a microtask queued ahead of admit still runs before the wasm put) with an optional real-Keyhive residual test; the window between the ring's generation and the island replica (fold the generation into admit, or name it at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges`>>); `proofVersion` bumps on every daemon-bag title (bump on proof-carrying titles alone, or compare board heads); the node wake test crosses no sync port and the browser test passes no `dyadLedger`; the epoch-free tamper control's reason pattern reads too broad; an aside grant re-verifies its KEL each pass (cache lineage per `record.sig`). Outside that diff, `open-browser-vessel.ts`'s `stands === true -> aside` reads inverted on its face; the every-reader sweep checks it. L.
* `L25` ''Vessel tags across `rotatePlace`'' (2026-11-05). The tag secret rests random per face (device-minted, a `D` record, `bundle: "stays"`, sealed under the face's FCK on the node and under the face's own tree on the browser, `browser-custody.ts`), never derived from the place seed (row7-s3a), so a place rotation leaves every face's tag standing, and no re-admission rides a rotation. Owed: the ward's threat model names "the root holder can mint its own second device" as out of scope; and a browser tab that clears its origin storage mints a fresh tag for a face it already joined, which reads as a new vessel, while the fold's view of that case stays owed. Before the rite. L.
* `L26` ''`S3`'s read residues'' (the co-sign reads, 2026-11-05). Swept on `row7-s3b` (alpha line, no back-compat): a browser face's sealed ward-key record from before the key moved under its own ward (`sealed/ward-sign/<group>`) stood on disk, read by nothing; the face's next tag ask now removes it. Owed, each red-first with its control: no act frees a tag, so a vessel that lost its atom never rejoins that face; the `signedInput` fallback after a lease roll; a seated admission with no linked edge still mints anew, while the fold refuses the duplicate tag, so no second seat stands; every face already on disk folds to zero devices, which fits no back-compat and re-genesis freely, and the `S3` land names it. The tag-secret reading against the 2026-10-19 ruling, the HKDF-under-a-TPM bar and the founding resume across a rotation closed by the per-face tag secret, row7-s3a; the rest build before the rite. L.
* `L27` ''`S2`'s read residues'' (the ward reads, 2026-11-05). A planted marker locks no root out and stands in for no card read-back (the waiver stands as an explicit, process-local harness seat in the process that reads the card); the harness refuses route seating when `found --storage` points elsewhere; a face route parked through the custody frame becomes a one-use, unguessable reference bound to a digest of its operation's identifying arguments; the ward digest folds a conflicting handle index; the harbor walk founds through its own seated route. Owed: re-measure the ward refusal that named no reason against `awaitOnRolled`, which carries no budget; a witness for Kahu-gated canon-bag projection (the harbor leg moved to crossroads). L.
* `L20` The fiction and art domains' o-takiage (#/rulings, 2026-11-01). Once the lararium stands, the RPG chapters and the concept art take wiki domains of their own under `edition/*` and `art/*` tag families, each with an o-takiage rite fitted to it and designed from the pono sweep; the domain sweep of 2026-11-01 found no RPG or art wiki yet, and lifecycle tags already read opt-in. The lares design laws never bind these families by default. Red: a carrier tagged `edition/*` passes `meme check` under its own family's law and meets no `lifecycle/*` gate it never opted into; control: a `lifecycle/designed` carrier in `bags/lares` still meets its gate. Waits on `L13`. L.
* `L31` ''The drop floor's named limits'' (`L23`, #/ashes; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seat-harness#/the-ward`>>). A writer that holds both custody and the board's local storage on a face with no sibling device can roll both back, so a single-device rollback still replays (a sibling's copy heals it at sync); a device that rotates its atom voids its own bound records until the hand commits them again (it fails closed); records signed before the floor carry no owner and void until recommitted (alpha, no back-compat); the re-read's text-edit and overwrite-then-delete cases read green only, with no red on base. The fork's other branch, a ward-signed ledger head, still falls to a whole-ledger rollback and makes a brake wait on the ward, so it stays unbuilt. L.

