!! Stride 2 Floor

Floor, wire and realm release shapes on the face and authority ground.

''Reading note'': the tree and git decide what stands (#/the-loops). Each item names the shape the tree holds today and what stays owed on it; landed work reads in git and #/ashes.

!!! Seven-league stride notes

* ''Research pair: the Keyhive substrate's contract'' (`W11`, filed after the seat). Its question: which substrate properties stand as contract and which shift by version, each needing a guard at run time. Lenses: dependency contract analysis / adversarial compatibility testing.
* ''Research pair: the knock's leak'' (`W10`; its answer moves the dial's bytes, so it lands before the bake). MEASURED (two traded rounds, then a Mu test on the web, 2026-10-26; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane`>> #/the-knock-reading): IK already stands, so a dialer proves itself before any verdict; the floor knock harms nothing the floor promises; on the sovereign route a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path learns which of the K gates sharing an address and route a dial selects, at most log2(K) bits per dial, never the face, the verdict or a sealed byte; no public-pin filter escapes that, and a secret selector costs per-Nexus key delivery and a causal re-key on every removal. The operator ruled (2026-10-26) that the sovereign promise leaves a pin-holding path reader outside it, so `W10` closes as a named leak, with more research owed later.

!!! The items

* `W26` The system wikis release and every other wiki reads the floor (#/rulings, 2026-10-16), under the architecture of #/rulings (2026-10-18), its shape and evidence at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane`>>. Its six slices stand. (1) Genesis carries the first floor, its manifest and one snapshot per house-canon bag by CID, and `@oracle` reads that floor by CID. (2) Each vessel's system, crossroads and realm pointers rest in its own `@catalog`, and nothing writes the shared `@oracle` after genesis (`oracle-doc-no-writer.test.ts`). (3) The founding lands the counted 1-of-1 Kahu admission for persona zero's group (`landFoundingAdmission`) and registers each house-canon bag as a realm bag of the hearth's realm under persona zero's per-Nexus key (`landKahuRealm`); `kahuCabalCanonAccess` has its production caller (`kahuReachSourceOf`); the keel mounts only what the realm names, the registered bag set and the `bags/` mirrors follow, and no catalog entry names a system bag. (4) The release (`floor-release`: body, CID, steward seal by a seated Kahu key, the cabal's high-impact approval of the manifest's exact bytes, the charter's epoch lineage), the chain fold, `lares nexus release`, the porch (`GET /floor/<Nexus AID>`, `/cas/<cid>` for the head's blobs), the browser's verified read, and the flow map's own `flow-pointer` domain. (5) The vessel pins the floor, one pin per (vessel, Nexus) in its control home, starting at genesis; `lares vessel floor status|accept` and the browser's `floorStatus` / `acceptFloor` answer through one mesh seam (`floor-pin`), the accept walking `prior` from the pin and refusing a non-descendant and a fork by name; the next mount stands on the accepted floor, and live wikis raise the reboot-pending alert (no island swaps its floor live yet). (6) One predicate (`requireKahuReach`) guards the residency reactor, meme put and delete, draft placement and a realm steward's write, and the keyholder island's verifier carries it for `--in-wiki` verbs. The house canon widens slices 1, 3 and 6 past `lares` and `lararium` to every disk-sourced holding but the board (#/rulings 2026-11-11). OWED: a browser Kahu hand rides the face context (the browser composes no board reader and reads as a stranger, fail closed); a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until that context carries the charter and the board to it, and `packages/lararium-node/src/commands/device-admit.ts` states the law; a joinee reads its hearth's floor by the release and its CIDs (slice 4), where slice 5's accept moves its vessel's pin; the carriage `canon` names (`admitCanonDocs` in that file, the browser's `hearth-canon`) read records nothing writes, and retire with this item. The vessel floor's further owed items rest in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane#/owed`>>. W.
* `W26-5/G` The page boots on its pin (the genesis collision read, 2026-11-05). A first arrival kindles from the house's own Pronaos (`/.well-known/lar`, `/genesis/seed.json`, seed-named `/genesis/cas/<cid>`), hashes the seed to the descriptor's CID and each member to its own, and mints its pin from them; the first arrival's trust in its own origin stands ruled, and the check reads as self-consistency, labelled so in every refusal. A vessel that holds a pin (a held `hearthTrueName` in its delegation edges, an accepted floor pin) boots only bytes that match it, from the hearth or any mirror by CID (a mirror carries, never kindles), and refuses a mismatch by name: `genesis-mismatch` with the expected CID, the served CID, the anchor compared against and the cure (`lares vessel rite rebuild`). The node's seed witness (`genesis-pin.json`, `L5`) refuses nothing (#/rulings, 2026-11-18, D1): a boot whose seed differs prints it as an offer (`[genesis seed] a newer seed waits: <ratchet words>`), the founding record keeps serving and nothing moves at boot, and only a torn witness refuses (`packages/lararium-node/src/genesis-resolve.ts`). The accept act (`W26` slice 5) moves the pin to a newer signed release by a person's own act; the genesis pin's crash window still blocks this item (#/side-lanes, the porch: a hearth with no pin serves `unpinned` on its descriptor, never silently). The page's self-consistency read stands (`genesis-mismatch`, `arrival-descriptor-missing`; `packages/lararium-web/src/genesis-anchor.ts`), and the pinned-vessel refusals stay owed. The release's floor card and anchor come in at the page's carriage door as the second channel. Open call: whether the release body names the seed CID, or the manifest widens to carry the genesis regions (a floor-manifest shape change that moves with the `X0` bake). Reds: a seed whose hash differs from the descriptor's refuses; a descriptor-less hearth refuses `arrival-descriptor-missing`, never a hang; a pinned vessel refuses a hearth that serves another genesis; a diverging `LAR_GENESIS` override boots on, its seed printed as an offer beside the seed witness; the built web dist carries no genesis copy (one source). Controls: equal bytes boot as today, and offline boot proves from held CAS. W.
* A floor read carries no as-of stamp: `standAs` returns a bare class (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor`>>).
* The hostful code half: `carrierBaseRelPath` discards a hostful URI (`bag-paths.ts`), so a hostful title never sites; one carrier claims otherwise (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/lar-uri-namespace`>>).
* `G20` Carried items, each now owned (kit `docs/pono/porch-lane`). Closed: the sensorium's tree-sitter pins (`tree-sitter==0.26.0`, ABI 15 inside its window, pinned by test) and the corpus round-trip, which now sweeps every carrier under `bags/` and fails by name on one skipped by shape. Ruled by the house on the porch's leans and owed in the porch kit's bundle four (`porch-lane#/what-stays`): road (iv) surfaces the derived impact set for review as information, while a quorum revokes by name; `/cas` lands and verifies the body before the public index names it. The loan's CID keying rides `P10`. `resolveBootDoc` waits on the writer's own flush, never a clock. The parallel-draft alert's persistence passes to the hands room. G.
* `P10` The vessel-side fetch door stands built (`makeCidResolver` beside `hermCasTransitFromEnv` in `open-node-vessel.ts`); the herm's own client leg waits on the explicit-Nexus herm relay, since a herm dials no hearth. One circle in the law stands beside it: a carrier may read a book its registration declares public, the declaration lives on the realm doc, and the realm doc never crosses to a carrier. The held red in `tests/e2e/herm-reshares-public-blob.e2e.test.ts` waits on both. Also owed: seeding a herm from a stood Lararium; and, carried from `G20` (house ruling on the porch's lean, 2026-10-27), a loan keys by CID, keeping holder and tier, once the loan carries a causal expiry counted in rolls or epochs, never a clock (`effect-record.ts` lists `loan` TTL-pending). House. Before the fence where the ceremony seeds a herm.
* `P11` Board migration beyond the persona log; the explicit DEPARTURE, named by an act at the rite and never inferred at a boot; the offering's announce and taker doors. May follow.
* `P12` A realm's edge board and vouch board cross by a lane of their own, and a fleet's edge board by the sibling lane; both composers have yet to seat those lanes (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges`>>). May follow.
* The Handle surface adapters: four surfaces stand as type and vocabulary; loopback first, then DNS control (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/handle-card`>>). `lares handle graft` stands as a stub over a built mint, where `publish`, `rotate`, `burn` and `attest` run live; the antigen's ban-`nym` move stays untouched; the browser's publish surface and a phone summons that presents the veil card stay owed. Flagged, unbuilt: a Handle's presenting cabal may also serve as its recovery cabal.
* `K9` The cadence lineage's seat events and its offer verifier; the joint founding's one cadence citation stands, and a household seed cites none (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract`>>). P, with the offers.
