* ''The reality tunnel's memory shore'': the tunnel declares no capture hook while the sensorium rests until the founded-Lararium proof, so the house's hooks folder carries none, and the three `*-hooks-owned` items have `tend` lift any host command that names a script there which no `[[home]]` item declares (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/cli/reality-tunnel#/the-tunnel`>>). The sensorium lane's capture hook joins as a `[[home]]` item when that lane wakes (`L44`) and reads the `lares hooks pause` marker first. Once the memory stage stands (`L13`), the shore decides whether a harness's own memory reads from the stage.
* ''The operator's declarations win'' (design unfinished): an operator's own choice outranks the tunnel on every home entry it names, so `tend` never overrides it. The entries that override today: retention (Codex's `history.persistence` and Copilot's `commandHistoryMaxSize` set whole, Claude's floor raising a lower `cleanupPeriodDays`), the `lares` bin link re-aiming a link the operator set on purpose, a prose line carrying the seed's link lifted whole, and a file left holding frontmatter alone deleted. Open: where a declaration rests (a home-side file the tunnel reads, or a mark per entry) and how `verify` reads an entry the operator holds (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/cli/reality-tunnel`>>).
* ''The CLI's test laws'': the pattern-integrity precedent train T builds on (#/stride-t-recut, `T18`); the lares CLI's suite re-cut as sixteen laws over the live tables, its literal bug-finds kept as seeds and its strength read by named mutants; every law stands built for at least one domain, and the doors each law has yet to reach stand named in its item (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/cli-test-laws#/the-laws`>>).
* ''DreamDOM, train D'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16: DreamDOM names the superset of cameras, every root template over every document sink across the one engine per wiki). The model stands whole in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom`>>; its phases `D0` to `D7` and items `D1` to `D17` read in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap`>>, and this carrier keeps no copy of them. `F8`'s control-event leg rides the roadmap's camera-contract phase.
