* ''The harness items after its batch'' (the harness batch and the lane's hand-back; one controller carries them, Codex first, each meeting the focus test before it opens). Before the harness moves in: N2 (a drained door's answer may carry truncated output, reaching only the lead); the check list validated at broker boot; the F1 socket probe run inside the real Codex wall (the blind read rated F1 on a walled lead listening on a unix socket in its worktree); `wait-marker.mjs`, a seat watcher as a tool that waits on an `fs.watch` event at the done marker or the pid, so no hand types an until loop; and the build-freshness lock's `mkdir`, which still follows a symlinked `.lares-build` (`build-freshness.ts`). After it moves in, with the measurement work: the capability manifest as one source that generates the launcher's arguments, the canon seat tables and the witness expectations, with a drift test (the lead's capabilities stood in three copies and two had drifted), its F11b acceptance probe first (an adversarial `virtualStoreDir`, `globalVirtualStoreDir` and `lockfileDir` under the real install wall). The lane state's `generation`, the cached-token measure, the deterministic controller, the F11b fence and the one-test e2e door rest in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seat-harness#/owed`>>. About ninety feedback memories wait for a retirement o-takiage after standing.
* ''The deps' tail'' (the deps before the founding, #/o-takiage): `smol-toml` 1.9.1 and `vite` 8.3.5 (rolldown 1.2.16) move the packed plugin bytes, so they ride the next genesis bake; `@keyhive/keyhive` holds 0.3.0-alpha.1 through the founding, its 0.6.0 port designed and held past it (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/keyhive-zero-six-port`>>), and a Keyhive move re-reads `W11`'s four alarms. The Playwright image pins its tag and its digest, and the image law (`tools/workflow-law.test.mjs`, WL3 to WL5) refuses any workflow that installs a browser or names an unpinned image.
* ''The legacy-check pyre'' (#/the-order, rank 27; #/rulings, 2026-11-01). Its gate opened: the house stood and the MCP seat answered (2026-11-13). ''R''s refusal of the retired trailer (`retired-trailer`) burns here. A Sonnet cold reader sorts every check across every era, in code, tests, witnesses, frozen fixtures and canon prose, seeded by ''Q''s keep-and-burn ledger: KEEP where it guards a live invariant and would catch a fresh mistake, BURN where it refuses only a spelling the tree no longer holds or blocks a person's legit choice, SPLIT where one part does each. Its known positive comes first: the `file-path` deny in the deserializer, its `meme check` red and its witness leg. A blind Opus security reader then reads each BURN entry with planted inputs on a scratch root, since a refusal of an old form can double as an injection or smuggling guard, and answers burn-safe, burn-with-replacement (naming the live invariant that replaces it) or keep-for-security. One lane then burns, red-first where a burn changes behaviour, under the whole witness fleet and full CI, as security class. The harvester burn stands; `retired-trailer` still stands in `lararium-memetic-frame/src/check.ts`, `span.ts` and `ingest-gate.ts`, owed to this lane. The operator's rulings (2026-11-01): //"hold to alpha evergreen & after all this lands o-takiage the checks that deny stale/legacy forms. Especially the file-path tiddler field wards (pono to purge them, but it would then block legit user choices if kept)."// and the alpha-line law that an old-name refusal lives ONE commit and then burns, with old-shape refusals and shape gates in source burning too. The cold reader's scope covers every era (code in `packages/**/src`, `tools/**` and the Python scripts; tests in `packages/**/tests`, `tests/e2e` and `tools/*.test.*`; witnesses, including the evergreen old-shape counts; frozen-fixture skips and frozen-only readers; canon prose naming retired forms). For each check it names file and line, what the check refuses, which era and rename made it, whether a LIVE input could still carry that form (a retired field or key name can return to user space), and a verdict KEEP, BURN or SPLIT; the table ranks BURN first and gives the burn order (a clause before its deny entry, tests with the code they guard). The known positive it must confirm first: the `file-path` deny (the deserializer's `META_DENY` roots and children, the `meme check` red, the `meme-coordinates-witness` leg) and the grammar cut's census classes. The Opus reader answers SHIP or HOLD on the burn list as a whole, then BURN-SAFE, BURN-WITH-REPLACEMENT or KEEP-FOR-SECURITY per entry, blind to the first reader's reasoning until it forms its own on the BURN entries' files. Both readers run read-only.
* ''The harness deep read'' (owed after standing, since it needs the live wiki server; #/the-order, rank 31): a deep read and debug pass over the landed seat harness once the wiki server stands.
* ''The Projection Loom'' (owed after standing, parked there by the operator; #/the-order, rank 31): it stays in the house (operator, 2026-11-18), reserved on `feature/projection-loom` (draft PR #222 into `develop`) for a deep refactor into a natively callable web3 capability after the founding and the hearth proof; its history rests at the tags `archive/loom/*` and `archive/pr84-markdown-pre-otakiage-20261031` (`864dc19e8`).
* ''The porch'', a standing hygiene lane beside the slots, each item red-first with its control:
** ''The genesis pin's crash window'' (`L5`'s tail): `pinGenesisSeed` removes and rewrites the pin with a plain write, never atomically (route it through `publishFile`); a crash between a founding's success and the pin write leaves a fresh vessel unpinned, and a non-force `found` skips without healing it (write the pin on the skipped path where none stands and the seed resolves shipped); the tests cover only the pre-custody refusal.
** ''The intent relay's cell order'' (`T19`'s tail, owned by `T6`'s boot pins): nothing behaviour-tests that the composer puts `intentRelayService` in its cell before the first sweep (`open-node-vessel.ts`), and the wired census passes a reverted order.
** ''A found over a standing home names the state'': `lares vessel found` over a standing custody home with no place key refuses "no key file ... run lares vessel found", advice that loops; the refusal names the state (a home stands without a place key: move it aside or restore it), never an old name.
** ''The compound rite and its help'' (the landmark map's collisions; a bounded build-seat lane before the pre-rite): `lares vessel rite founding` halts only on a nonzero exit while `stand` exits zero on a failed payload, so a failed stand flows on into seed; the help names bare `found` then `persona new 0`, where only `found --hearth` seats the charter and persona zero; the founding runbook's separate `persona new 0` line trues with it. The dogfood stand and the keeper rite both run the primitives, never the compound.
** ''The persona-root matcher'': the pattern no longer matches a leading-zero index (`-h01`); confirm no writer emits one, else widen the matcher.
** ''A silent-zero instrument'': `node tools/two-phase-boot.test.mjs` run directly exits 0 on a failure (a bare `process.exit()` in its `finally`); `node --test`, the CI glob, reports it.
** ''A runaway inside one file'' (VSCode-TW5-Syntax `tools/composition-check.js`, Lares-Awakens' side): the check misses a runaway that starts inside one file, so the seed read zero failures while broken (2026-11-01); a planted single-file runaway reds it first.
** ''VSCode-TW5-Syntax 3.0.3'' (deferred past the 3.0.2 release; Lares-Awakens' list rides the submodule's branch): on the house side, `api/mu.mem` line 14 writes `->>>`, which reads clearer as `-> >>`, a canon re-cut the house owns; on the submodule's side, the rest of the list, with the long-standing multi-line `~~` strikethrough divergence (older than ''R'') beside it.
** ''The holder venv's cache key'' (`L3`'s tail): `ci.yml` and `e2e-shards.yml` key the cached `~/.venv` on `mempalace/pyproject.toml` and the sensorium requirements alone, so a mempalace submodule commit or a Python patch release reuses a stale venv; the key takes the submodule's commit and the interpreter's full version.
** ''The veil reader'': `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/worldline_veil.py` expects a persona root in the clear at the identity root, while roots now rest encrypted per face, so it reads nothing; a sensorium porch item.
** ''The carried-Nexus rig's notes'' (`T19`'s and `T27`'s tails): `T19`'s `chmod 000` case bites nothing under root (a false red alone); `seatStranger` leaks its dial when the seat fails; `T27`'s rig waits a fixed 3 s settle window.
** ''Faces whose keys open after boot'' (`T33`'s tail): a face the vessel holds but does not wear gets its ledger classed vessel-private only when it mounts, so its frontier pins and seen entries stay reachable through a realm alias until then (its marks still need receipts); the cure reads atom keys before custody opens.

!!! Off this road, held by name
* ''Grammar'': tangle, the putback law and the tongue fold wait on a real return trip and a whole regeneration of `packages/tree-sitter-memetic-wikitext` against the released grammar; that regeneration also unlocks publication. A relay-stream profile (the SYN-framed batch), a carrier seal with a computed check, and EOT targeting stay held in reserve. The grammar watch reads in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/grammar-watch`>>.
* ''Publication'': the `text/markdown; variant=memetic-markdown` registration, the provisional `lar` scheme after `lar-uri` gains its Security section, the vendor media type, and the drafts. The standalone plugin artifact ships from `packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/standalone/`.
* ''The live wiki's floors'': exercise the quoteblock floor at both grains, the child gate and the persisted parallel drafts against real concurrent browser saves, and turn every surprise into a test.
* ''A standing whole-tree gate'' runs as a spirit pass, never as a CLI verb or a trigger.
* ''The ahi-kā knobs'' (the hysteresis gap, the commons-against-hearth exemption) wait on an estimator fit; no ruling stands owed.
* ''Future vessels'' (native mobile, Mudlet, Unreal) enter one at a time, each declaring whether it hosts a sovereign vessel or attaches a surface to a named one. Each enters as a DreamDOM surface: a root template over a document sink, its two-way capability rated by name (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom#/the-superset`>>), on train D's lean or wider phases.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/fresh-start`>>

!! The fresh start ~ by hand, reversible, never a command

NO pave or wipe command stands (operator-ruled): such a command carries too much risk. In early alpha a fresh
START still reads pono when it runs BY HAND: MOVE the old homes aside — rename them, never delete them, so
the move stays reversible — then found fresh on the re-found build. Valuable data lives in git, in the
private `claude-backup` repository, or on `D:`; a vessel home holds nothing that only it holds.

A fresh machine needs no move: a fresh vessel seeds from the tracked `bags/` and the committed `genesis/`
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/fresh-state`).

The homes to move: the ones the OLD build's resolvers name — the `~/.lares` home, the XDG data homes for
`lares` and `lararium`, and the state home — asked of the old build at the moment of moving, never
enumerated by hand. A founding refuses a store that holds carriers no slot tree commits to (`OccupiedStoreRefusal`, before any
route gets asked and before any write), which keeps an accidental founding off any home left unmoved. Other
Nexuses rejoin through presented admits; every old admit names an old AID and reads dead by construction.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/open`>>

!! Open ~ what the operator owns

!!! Seats, custody and recovery
# ''Recovery contacts and recovery.'' The enrolment shape stands ruled (#/rulings). Request authentication, the veto, a person's death and succession, the catastrophe rite and any third key, and a Handle's DNS binding stand open at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/seed-and-nexus`>>.
# ''A sealed receipt manifest for carriage.'' It would let a root restored from paper re-open its carriage after device loss — and would turn carriage toward the backup W rules it never becomes. The lenses split; re-opening W needs the operator's turned key.
# ''Carriage across leaves.'' A guest-held carry-claim proven at the carry door would let carriage follow a guest across leaves — a second relation and a second domain. Lean: not built.
# ''The reading of "delegated keys" for cloud carriers'', deferred until the operator can deploy to a cloud surface (#/the-road).
# ''After-founding comms for non-Claude seats'': lane-message tiddlers on the daemon wiki, read and written through lane capabilities, ride #/the-order, rank 31, and never gate a founding.
# ''A kāpae over a top-only title'' (`L37`, `recipe-layer-model#/delete-reveals-or-shadows`). A kāpae over a title that stood ONLY in the top layer hides any copy that later arrives beneath. Default, carried until the operator rules: kāpae stays the default everywhere, since it guards against a concurrent copy resurrecting the record and every door already raises one; the consequence names the hiding, and `L38`'s lower door gives a hand the way back.
# ''The confirm gate's shape'' (#/rulings, 2026-11-13). The operator's note asks the gate; the house's lean names its shape (the passphrase where the vessel holds custody, the typed phrase at a bare floor, the platform's own clear beyond any house door, the class as every door that destroys a place or a face). The browser stands built as leaned (`C4`); a locked vessel verifies a passphrase by the unwrap alone against the trees at rest. Open beside it: the passkey and paper routes at the gate, and whether any tree that opens narrows to the place tree.
# ''House leans the operator may overturn'': the floor vessel key drops its next-key commitment; the long-silent device rule; the strangers' dial drops the newest arrival (#/decisions); the seal's standing leans (`S7` of #/stride-1-spine).

!!! Planes and offerings
# ''The offering's `offer` and `witness` caps'' against the Lamplighter stack.
# ''The crossing record.'' Its durable emission threshold (lean: authority, vessel, federation and externally meaningful-effect boundaries alone), and whether a destination receipt always signs separately (lean: yes).
# ''Engine cadence'': who holds a cadence share and the epoch pin stand ruled (#/rulings); whether partial conformance lands before `kahuli engine` un-holds (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract`>>).
# ''Grammar submissions'': whether the Nexus Kahu or the corpus-kahu receive them.
# ''DNS custody past the credential'': delegated `_acme-challenge`, record custody, the ACME account and CAA travel as one question (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/bounded-reach-contract`>>). With it: whether a host timer or a hand runs renewal, and the answer for a phone that forces encrypted DNS.
# ''The crossroads mirror's filter'' (`G21` of #/operator-gates).
# ''Removal's reach.'' The model stands ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges`>>). Five questions stay the operator's, each with the house's lean. Whether an edge act may ever use the emergency class (lean: never). Whether a seated member under a member shadow keeps a seat's signature until the next roll (lean: yes, a seat leaves by a roll alone). What a recovery council holds after a mutual removal (lean: nothing built; the fork stands as the one exit). Whether a holder's key reads at its log's current head, so a recovered face keeps its edges (lean: yes, owed with the resolver of #/side-lanes). Whether a counted raise moves the keys while a lift still races it (lean: yes, remove-wins reaches the keys, and a lift then seats afresh). Two more came with the key side. What removes a seat no standing hand can revoke, the founding vessel's own among them (lean: a fresh group, at the re-founding that moves the PersonaGroup to a Keyhive group). Whether a vessel that holds no revoke authority goes on trying a raise until it sees the seat leave (lean: yes, and each try hands the roll on again, so the content key rolls whoever revokes the seat).
# ''The self-slot inner ring.'' Wiring it freezes a naming: a bag URL through a live ring hashes to seed its document, and a re-name costs a re-founding. Lean: widen the bridge first, and wire the ring on an explicit ruling alone.

!!! Shore, grammar and code
# ''The ungated slot child.'' A slot child's native save never grades; three child-edit shapes stand marked as the operator's call (`packages/lararium-tw5/tests/meme-backstop.test.ts`; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/syncer-back-parity`>>).
# ''Ruling-gated mesh modules'' (listed in the header of `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts`): `recipe`, `readiness`, `reaction-graph`, `pronaos`, `offering-inspection`. Each moves or stays by ruling alone.
# ''The capture cell'' sits apart for review in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-node/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/capture/` and `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/capture/`. Canon places capture in Python per stream with the TS daemon coordinating alone (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model`>>), while the TS cell carries the live path. Rule: retire it to Python, or re-home it.
# ''Receipt names and verb capabilities.'' Whether a receipt's address follows the house's own kind nouns or the content-addressed surface; and the table that maps each routed verb to its capability, where `deriveRoutedCap` answers for every routed verb today (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-local-dispatch.ts`).
# ''Rulings that rest in their own carriers'': the promotion receipt's fields (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/canon-boundary`>>), the one-of-one mantle (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/handle-card`>>), the lease's questions (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/realm-bag-brief`>>), and the offering's questions (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/heraldry`>>).
# ''Two Kairoses.'' The fiction names KAIROS as a watcher that speaks unasked; the code's Kairos pet-names an unbuilt entity that refreshes an OAuth grant at the right moment (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/reach-plane`>>). One entity, or two that share a name?
# ''Alerts and shadows.'' Whether a disk conflict that arrives while no wiki stands pinned raises its alert at the next pin; whether a hand that deletes its override of a shadow leaves a delete, where today the shadow's text gets saved as a record; whether the page warns when a browser has joined no face.
# ''The confirm door upstream.'' The fork asks its questions through the wiki itself (`$tw.utils.confirm`, `tm-confirm`). Owed before a donation: the order of actions after a confirm, a switch for a blocking prompt, and one squashed change. The withdrawn render boundary's upstream pull request, if it still stands open, advertises a design the fork backed out.
# ''The realm consult's root map'' (`peerContractNymMap`, `open-node-vessel.ts`): a seat held by <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/two-maps`>> and the house ruling of 2026-10-16 (#/rulings, a realm's steward map holds leaves), filled only by a root edge proven at the seat. Nothing fills it today and its readers fail closed. The house leans keep it and name an owed item for its filler (`T29` states its law).
# ''The barrel re-exported names'' (487): they wait on their own ruling before `T4`'s sweep reaches them.
# ''One sentence for the `CLAUDE.md` adapter note'', the operator's to place: the CLI's ingest, watch and REPACK derive against `LAR_BAGS` and `LAR_WIKIS`, so "read neither" holds for the daemon's projection mirrors alone.

